helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id5181432				0	lv	Charts can be based on the following data:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7787102				0	lv	Spreadsheet values from Calc cell ranges				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7929929				0	lv	Cell values from a Writer table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id4727011				0	lv	Values that you enter in the Chart Data Table dialog (you can create these charts in Writer, Draw, or Impress, and you can copy and paste them also to Calc)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id76601				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Creates a chart in the current document. To use a continuous range of cells as the data source for your chart, click inside the cell range, and then choose this command. Alternatively, select some cells and choose this command to create a chart of the selected cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
