helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	lv	The Tools bar contains frequently used functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151242				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/02/03010000.xhp\" name=\"Formula Cursor\"\>Formula Cursor\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Welcome to the $[officename] Math Help				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148868				0	lv	Welcome to the $[officename] Math Help				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153915				0	lv	How to Work With $[officename] Math				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143229				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091500.xhp\" name=\"Formula Reference Tables\"\>Formula Reference Tables\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153808				0	lv	$[officename] Math Menus, Toolbars, and Keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143269				0	lv	Have a look at \<link href=\"http://www.dmaths.org\"\>www.dmaths.org\</link\> for a set of additional %PRODUCTNAME Math icons and macros.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156396				0	lv	Help about the Help				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0102.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Edit				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156385				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/main0102.xhp\" name=\"Edit\"\>Edit\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	lv	The commands in this menu are used to edit formulas. In addition to basic commands, (for example, copying contents) there are functions specific to $[officename] Math such as searching for placeholders or errors.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Menus				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149021				0	lv	\<variable id=\"main0100\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/main0100.xhp\" name=\"Menus\"\>Menus\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	lv	The menu bar contains all the commands for working with $[officename] Math. It contains a list of all the available operators as well as the commands for editing, viewing, arranging, formatting and printing formula documents and the objects contained in them. Most of the menu commands are only available when you are creating or editing a formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0105.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149121				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/main0105.xhp\" name=\"Format\"\>Format\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	lv	This menu contains commands needed to format formulas.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156385				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/05010000.xhp\" name=\"Fonts\"\>Fonts\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154656				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Font Size\"\>Font Size\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154484				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/05030000.xhp\" name=\"Spacing\"\>Spacing\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151242				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/05040000.xhp\" name=\"Alignment\"\>Alignment\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0107.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Window				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155066				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/main0107.xhp\" name=\"Window\"\>Window\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0107.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	lv	In the Window menu, you can open a new window and see the document list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0106.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Tools				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149019				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/main0106.xhp\" name=\"Tools\"\>Tools\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	lv	Use this menu to open and edit the symbol catalog, or import an external formula as a data file or via clipboard. The program interface can be adjusted to meet your requirements. You can also change the program options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/06020000.xhp#importfile\" name=\"Import Formula\"\>Import Formula\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/06020000.xhp#importclipboard\" name=\"Import MathML\"\>Import MathML from Clipboard\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145385				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Customize\"\>Customize\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0103.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	View				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155064				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/main0103.xhp\" name=\"View\"\>View\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	lv	Sets the display scale and defines which elements you want to be visible. Most of the commands that you can enter into the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window can also be accessed through a mouse click if you have already opened the Elements window with \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"View - Elements\"\>\<emph\>View - Elements\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/03010000.xhp\" name=\"Zoom\"\>Zoom\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Toolbars				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149121				0	lv	\<variable id=\"main0200\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/main0200.xhp\" name=\"Toolbars\"\>Toolbars\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	lv	The default toolbars available when working with an activated formula document in $[officename] Math are described here. You can customize the toolbars to meet your requirements by moving, deleting or adding new icons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	$[officename] Math Features				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155064				0	lv	\<variable id=\"main0503\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/main0503.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Math Features\"\>$[officename] Math Features\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3156386				0	lv	This section contains an overview of some of the important functions and capabilities that $[officename] Math offers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3148486				0	lv	$[officename] Math provides numerous operators, functions and formatting assistants to help you create formulas. These are all listed in a selection window, in which you can click the required element with the mouse to insert the object into your work. There is an exhaustive \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091500.xhp\" name=\"reference\"\>reference\</link\> list and numerous \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090900.xhp\" name=\"samples\"\>samples\</link\> contained in the Help.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	lv	Creating a Formula				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3145386				0	lv	As with charts and images, formulas are created as objects within a document. Inserting a formula into a document automatically starts $[officename] Math. You can create, edit and format the formula using a large selection of predefined symbols and functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153916				0	lv	Typing a Formula Directly				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	lv	If you are familiar with the $[officename] Math language, you can also type a formula directly into the document. For example, type this formula into a text document: "a sup 2 + b sup 2 = c sup 2". Select this text and choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - Formula\</emph\>. The text will be converted into a formatted formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3146325				0	lv	Formulas cannot be calculated in $[officename] Math because it is a formula editor (for writing and showing formulas) and not a calculation program. Use spreadsheets to calculate formulas, or for simple calculations use the text document calculation function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145829				0	lv	Creating a Formula in the Commands Window				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3153001				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_COMMAND_WIN_EDIT\"\>Use the $[officename] Math Commands window to enter and edit formulas. As you make entries in the Commands window, you see the results in the document.\</ahelp\> To maintain an overview when creating long and complicated formulas, use the Formula Cursor on the Tools bar. When this function is activated, the cursor location within the Commands window is also shown in the text window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150014				0	lv	Individual Symbols				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3145246				0	lv	You can create your own symbols and import characters from other fonts. You can add new symbols to the basic catalog of $[officename] Math symbols, or create your own special catalogs. Numerous special characters are also available.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148392				0	lv	Formulas in Context				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	lv	To make working with formulas easier, use the context menus, which can be called up with a right mouse click. This applies especially to the Commands window. This context menu contains all the commands that are found in the Elements window, and also operators, and so on, which can be inserted into your formula by mouse-click without having to key them into the Commands window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/main0101.xhp\" name=\"File\"\>File\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\main0101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	lv	This menu contains the general commands for working with formula documents, such as open, save and print.				20200411 15:09:53
