helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090401.xhp	0	help	par_id3148946				0	lv	\<emph\>Parameter:\</emph\> Parameters to pass to the procedure. The type and number of parameters is dependent on the routine that is executing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090401.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	lv	A keyword is optional when you call a procedure. If a function is executed as an expression, the parameters must be enclosed by brackets in the statement. If a DLL is called, it must first be specified in the \<emph\>Declare-Statement\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
