helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090302.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	lv	Use the GoTo statement to instruct $[officename] Basic to continue program execution at another place within the procedure. The position must be indicated by a label. To set a label, assign a name, and then and end it with a colon (":").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090302.xhp	0	help	par_id3155416				0	lv	You cannot use the GoTo statement to jump out of a Sub or Function.				20200411 15:09:53
