helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	lv	Calculates the cosine of an angle. The angle is specified in radians. The result lies between -1 and 1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	lv	Using the angle Alpha, the Cos-Function calculates the ratio of the length of the side that is adjacent to the angle, divided by the length of the hypotenuse in a right-angled triangle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154141				0	lv	Cos(Alpha) = Adjacent/Hypotenuse				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125				0	lv	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145172				0	lv	Cos (Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156214				0	lv	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	lv	Double				20200411 15:09:53
