helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Date and Time Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150502				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030000.xhp\" name=\"Date and Time Functions\"\>Date and Time Functions\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153255				0	lv	Use the statements and functions described here to perform date and time calculations.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	lv	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Basic lets you calculate time or date differences by converting the time and date values to continuous numeric values. After the difference is calculated, special functions are used to reconvert the values to the standard time or date formats.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	lv	You can combine date and time values into a single floating-decimal number. Dates are converted to integers, and times to decimal values. \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Basic also supports the variable type Date, which can contain a time specification consisting of both a date and time.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Open Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>Open statement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020103.xhp\" name=\"Open Statement [Runtime]\"\>Open Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150769				0	lv	Opens a data channel.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230				0	lv	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124				0	lv	Open FileName As String [For Mode] [Access IOMode] [Protected] As [#]FileNumber As Integer [Len = DatasetLength]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	lv	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132	6			0	lv	\<emph\>FileName: \</emph\>Name and path of the file that you wan to open. If you try to read a file that does not exist (Access = Read), an error message appears. If you try to write to a file that does not exist (Access = Write), a new file is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	lv	\<emph\>Mode:\</emph\> Keyword that specifies the file mode. Valid values: Append (append to sequential file), Binary (data can be accessed by bytes using Get and Put), Input (opens data channel for reading), Output (opens data channel for writing), and Random (edits relative files).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	lv	\<emph\>IOMode:\</emph\> Keyword that defines the access type. Valid values: Read (read-only), Write (write-only), Read Write (both).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	lv	\<emph\>Protected:\</emph\> Keyword that defines the security status of a file after opening. Valid values: Shared (file may be opened by other applications), Lock Read (file is protected against reading), Lock Write (file is protected against writing), Lock Read Write (denies file access).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	lv	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> Any integer expression from 0 to 511 to indicate the number of a free data channel. You can then pass commands through the data channel to access the file. The file number must be determined by the FreeFile function immediately before the Open statement.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115				0	lv	\<emph\>DatasetLength:\</emph\> For random access files, set the length of the records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	lv	You can only modify the contents of a file that was opened with the Open statement. If you try to open a file that is already open, an error message appears.				20200411 15:09:53
