helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	File I/O Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156344				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020000.xhp\" name=\"File I/O Functions\"\>File I/O Functions\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	lv	Use File I/O functions to create and manage user-defined (data) files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	lv	You can use these functions to support the creation of "relative" files, so that you can save and reload certain records by specifying their record number. File I/O functions can also help you manage your files by providing you with information such as file size, current path settings, or the creation date of a file or a directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Display Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010100.xhp\" name=\"Display Functions\"\>Display Functions\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	lv	This section describes Runtime functions used to output information to the screen display.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	InStr Function [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155934				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>InStr function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155934				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03120401.xhp\" name=\"InStr Function [Runtime]\"\>InStr Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	par_id3153990				0	lv	Returns the position of a string within another string.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303				0	lv	The Instr function returns the position at which the match was found. If the string was not found, the function returns 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145090				0	lv	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	lv	InStr ([Start As Long,] Text1 As String, Text2 As String[, Compare])				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538				0	lv	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763				0	lv	Integer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148473				0	lv	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	9			0	lv	\<emph\>Start: \</emph\>A numeric expression that marks the position in a string where the search for the specified substring starts. If you omit this parameter, the search starts at the first character of the string. The maximum allowed value is 65535.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	lv	\<emph\>Text1:\</emph\> The string expression that you want to search.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	lv	\<emph\>Text2:\</emph\> The string expression that you want to search for.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	lv	\<emph\>Compare:\</emph\> Optional numeric expression that defines the type of comparison. The value of this parameter can be 0 or 1. The default value of 1 specifies a text comparison that is not case-sensitive. The value of 0 specifies a binary comparison that is case-sensitive.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	lv	To avoid a run-time error, do not set the Compare parameter if the first return parameter is omitted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154366				0	lv	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120401.xhp	0	help	par_id3154217				0	lv	Sub ExamplePosition				20200411 15:09:53
