helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020302.xhp\" name=\"Loc Function [Runtime]\"\>Loc Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	lv	Returns the current position in an open file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156422				0	lv	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768				0	lv	Loc(FileNumber)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	lv	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	lv	Long				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152462				0	lv	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	lv	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that contains the file number that is set by the Open statement for the respective file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	lv	If the Loc function is used for an open random access file, it returns the number of the last record that was last read or written.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115				0	lv	For a sequential file, the Loc function returns the position in a file divided by 128. For binary files, the position of the last read or written byte is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01050100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Watch Window				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149457				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/01050100.xhp\"\>Watch Window\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	lv	The Watch window allows you to observe the value of variables during the execution of a program. Define the variable in the Watch text box. Click on \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/02/11080000.xhp\"\>Enable Watch\</link\> to add the variable to the list box and to display its values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145173				0	lv	Watch				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BASICIDE_WATCHWINDOW_EDIT\"\>Enter the name of the variable whose value is to be monitored.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148645				0	lv	Remove Watch				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BASICIDE_REMOVEWATCH\"\>Removes the selected variable from the list of watched variables.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3152460\" src=\"res/baswatr.png\" width=\"0.25inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152460\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	lv	Remove Watch				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491				0	lv	Editing the Value of a Watched Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BASICIDE_WATCHWINDOW_LIST\"\>Displays the list of watched variables. Click twice with a short pause in between on an entry to edit its value.\</ahelp\> The new value will be taken as the variable's value for the program.				20200411 15:09:53
