helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	lv	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that contains the serial date number that is used to determine the month of the year.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770	9			0	lv	This function is the opposite of the \<emph\>DateSerial \</emph\>function. It returns the month in the year that corresponds to the serial date that is generated by \<emph\>DateSerial\</emph\> or \<emph\>DateValue\</emph\>. For example, the expression				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	lv	Print Month(DateSerial(1994, 12, 20))				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	lv	returns the value 12.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146923				0	lv	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	lv	Sub ExampleMonth				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	lv	MsgBox "" & Month(Now) ,64,"The current month"				20200411 15:09:53
