helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154347				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020404.xhp\" name=\"Dir Function [Runtime]\"\>Dir Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	lv	Returns the name of a file, a directory, or all of the files and the directories on a drive or in a directory that match the specified search path.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154365				0	lv	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3156282				0	lv	Dir [(Text As String) [, Attrib As Integer]]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156424				0	lv	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3153193				0	lv	String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153770				0	lv	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3161831				0	lv	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any string expression that specifies the search path, directory or file. This argument can only be specified the first time that you call the Dir function. If you want, you can enter the path in \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/00000002.xhp\" name=\"URL notation\"\>URL notation\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	9			0	lv	\<emph\>Attrib: \</emph\>Any integer expression that specifies bitwise file attributes. The Dir function only returns files or directories that match the specified attributes. You can combine several attributes by adding the attribute values:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	lv	0 : Normal files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	lv	16 : Returns the name of the directory only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3153952				0	lv	Use this attribute to check if a file or directory exists, or to determine all files and folders in a specific directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156				0	lv	To check if a file exists, enter the complete path and name of the file. If the file or directory name does not exist, the Dir function returns a zero-length string ("").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012	18			0	lv	To generate a list of all existing files in a specific directory, proceed as follows: The first time you call the Dir function, specify the complete search path for the files, for example, "D:\\Files\\*.sxw". If the path is correct and the search finds at least one file, the Dir function returns the name of the first file that matches the search path. To return additional file names that match the path, call Dir again, but with no arguments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3147348				0	lv	To return directories only, use the attribute parameter. The same applies if you want to determine the name of a volume (for example, a hard drive partition)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154942				0	lv	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
