helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Seek Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159413				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>Seek statement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159413				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020305.xhp\" name=\"Seek Statement [Runtime]\"\>Seek Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	lv	Sets the position for the next writing or reading in a file that was opened with the Open statement.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id2100589				0	lv	For random access files, the Seek statement sets the number of the next record to be accessed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id5444807				0	lv	For all other files, the Seek statement sets the byte position at which the next operation is to occur.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	lv	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020103.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020304.xhp\" name=\"Seek\"\>Seek\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	lv	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	lv	Seek[#FileNumber], Position (As Long)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154321				0	lv	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3153952	9			0	lv	\<emph\>FileNumber: \</emph\>The data channel number used in the Open statement.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366	10			0	lv	\<emph\>Position: \</emph\>Position for the next writing or reading. Position can be a number between 1 and 2,147,483,647. According to the file type, the position indicates the number of the record (files in the Random mode) or the byte position (files in the Binary, Output, Append or Input mode). The first byte in a file is position 1, the second byte is position 2, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	ChDrive Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>ChDrive statement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020402.xhp\" name=\"ChDrive Statement [Runtime]\"\>ChDrive Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	lv	Changes the current drive.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154138				0	lv	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685				0	lv	ChDrive Text As String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	lv	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	par_id3145172				0	lv	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any string expression that contains the drive letter of the new drive. If you want, you can use \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/00000002.xhp\" name=\"URL notation\"\>URL notation\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	lv	The drive must be assigned a capital letter. Under Windows, the letter that you assign the drive is restricted by the settings in LASTDRV. If the drive argument is a multiple-character string, only the first letter is relevant. If you attempt to access a non-existent drive, an error occurs that you can respond to with the OnError statement.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153188				0	lv	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	par_id3151113				0	lv	Sub ExampleCHDrive				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	lv	ChDrive "D" REM Only possible if a drive 'D' exists.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020402.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	lv	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
