helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149182				0	lv	\<variable id=\"insert_control\"\>\<link href=\"text/sbasic/guide/insert_control.xhp\" name=\"Creating Controls in the Dialog Editor\"\>Creating Controls in the Dialog Editor\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797	2			0	lv	Use the tools on the \<emph\>Toolbox \</emph\>of the BASIC dialog editor to add controls to your dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	lv	To open the \<emph\>Toolbox\</emph\>, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Insert Controls\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	lv	Click a tool on the toolbar, for example, \<emph\>Button\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	lv	On the dialog, drag the button to the size you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\control_properties.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Changing the Properties of Controls in the Dialog Editor				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\control_properties.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145786				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>properties; controls in dialog editor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;control properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls;changing properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dialog editor;changing control properties\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\control_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145786				0	lv	\<variable id=\"control_properties\"\>\<link href=\"text/sbasic/guide/control_properties.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Properties of Controls in the Dialog Editor\"\>Changing the Properties of Controls in the Dialog Editor\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\control_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	lv	You can set the properties of control that you add to a dialog. For example, you can change the color, name, and size of a button that you added. You can change most control properties when you create or edit a dialog. However, you can only change some properties at runtime.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\control_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	lv	To change the properties of a control in design mode, right-click the control, and then choose \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
