helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148731				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:LayoutStatus\"\>Displays the current Page Style. Double-click to edit the style, right-click to select another style.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283	3			0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Double-click the\<emph\> Page Style field \</emph\>to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040000.xhp\" name=\"Page Style\"\>Page Style\</link\> dialog, in which you can edit the style for the current page. In the context menu of this field, you can apply a Page Style. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151234	4			0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>Double-click the \<emph\>Page Style\</emph\> field to open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070000.xhp\" name=\"Page Style\"\>Page Style\</link\> dialog, in which you can edit the style for the current page. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	5			0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>Double-click this field to open the \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"Page Style\"\>Slide Design\</link\> dialog in which you can select the style for the current slide. You can select a different paper format or background. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	6			0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>Double-click this field to open the \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"Page Style\"\>Slide Design\</link\> dialog in which you select the style for the current page. You can select a different paper format or background. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Highlighting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/02160000.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting\"\>Highlighting\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	lv	\<variable id=\"zeichenhintergrundtext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BackColor\"\>Applies the current highlight color to the background of a text selection. If no text is selected, click the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, select the text that you want to highlight, and then click the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon again. To change the highlight color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, and then click the color that you want.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152551				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3149177\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_backcolor.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149177\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147210				0	lv	Highlighting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	lv	To Apply Highlighting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar, click the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10736				0	lv	To change the highlighting color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, and then click the color that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073E				0	lv	Select the text that you want to highlight.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	lv	To apply highlighting to a single word, double-click the word.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10757				0	lv	To turn off highlighting, press Esc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075A				0	lv	To Remove Highlighting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	lv	Select the highlighted text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149784				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, and then click \<emph\>No Fill\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Insert Database Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147000				0	lv	Insert Database Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SbaBrwInsert\"\>\<variable id=\"datenintext\"\>Inserts all fields of the marked record into the current document at the cursor position.\</variable\>\</ahelp\> The icon is only visible if the current document is a text document or a spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154186				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3147291\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbabrwinsert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147291\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	lv	Data to Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577	4			0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>In the data source browser, select the record that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon. The record is inserted in the document at the cursor position, with the contents of each individual field of the record copied to a table column. You can also select multiple records and transfer them into the document by clicking the \<emph\>Data to Text \</emph\>icon. Each individual record is then written to a new row.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	5			0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In the data source browser, select the records that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon, or drag-and-drop data from the data source browser into the document. This opens the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog. Select whether the data should be inserted as a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070100.xhp\" name=\"table\"\>table\</link\>, as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070200.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> or as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070300.xhp\" name=\"text\"\>text\</link\>.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	6			0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The preferences you set in the\<emph\> Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog are saved and will be active the next time the dialog is called. This save process is independent of the database and can record the preferences for a maximum of 5 databases.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326				0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If data is inserted into the document as a table, the table properties are not saved along with the data in the document. If you select the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> function for formatting the table, $[officename] will note the name of the format template. This template will then be used automatically if you insert data as a table again, unless the preferences have been changed.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Selection Mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148668				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>selection modes in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; selection modes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extension mode in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>additional selection mode\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>block selection mode\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148668				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/20050000.xhp\" name=\"Selection Mode\"\>Selection Mode\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146130				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:StatusSelectionMode\"\>Displays the current selection mode. You can switch between STD = Standard, EXT = Extend, ADD = Add, BLK = Block selection.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153894				0	lv	Each click in the field cycles through the available options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	lv	\<emph\>Display\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	lv	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155941				0	lv	\<emph\>Effect\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	lv	STD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	lv	Standard mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	lv	Click in text where you want to position the cursor; click in a cell to make it the active cell. Any other selection is then deselected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763				0	lv	EXT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	lv	Extension mode (F8)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153717				0	lv	Clicking in the text extends or crops the current selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	lv	ADD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147620				0	lv	Additional selection mode (Shift+F8)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307				0	lv	A new selection is added to an existing selection. The result is a multiple selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id7234717				0	lv	BLK				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6971037				0	lv	Block selection mode (\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F8)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id5258644				0	lv	A block of text can be selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id4441663				0	lv	On Windows systems, you can hold down the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Alt\</item\> key while dragging to select a block of text. You don't need to enter the block selection mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Date				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146902				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/20100000.xhp\" name=\"Date\"\>Date\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154926				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CurrentDate\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Displays the current date.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151299				0	lv	Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156183				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>database contents; inserting as tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156183	18			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_AS_TABLE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts data selected from the data source browser into the document as a table.\</ahelp\>In the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> option to insert the selected data into the document as a table. In the dialog, you can decide which database fields or columns are transferred, and how the text table is formatted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152594				0	lv	Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152918				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> area, use the arrow keys to select the columns of the database table that you want to apply to the text table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156042				0	lv	Database columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425	20			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_TBL_DB_COLUMN\"\>Specifies the database columns to be inserted into the text table.\</ahelp\> All database table columns that have not been accepted in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box are listed here. The entries are sorted alphabetically. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147577				0	lv	Table column(s)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_TABLE_COL\"\>Lists all database columns to be inserted into the document.\</ahelp\> A column will be assigned to each corresponding entry in the table. The entry order in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box determines the data order in the text table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146958				0	lv	>>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149750				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_ALL_TO\"\>Moves all listed database fields into the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box.\</ahelp\> All fields listed in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box are inserted into the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163802				0	lv	>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153662	23			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_ONE_TO\"\>Moves the selected database field into the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box. \</ahelp\> You can also double click an entry to move it to the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box. All fields listed in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box are inserted into the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149732				0	lv	<				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685	24			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_ONE_FROM\"\>Removes the selected database field from the\<emph\> Table column(s)\</emph\> list box\</ahelp\> The removed field is not inserted into the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771				0	lv	<<				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_ALL_FROM\"\>Removes all database fields from the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399				0	lv	Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154380				0	lv	Specifies the format for inserting the database fields into the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329				0	lv	From database				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_DBFMT_FROM_DB\"\>Accepts the database formats.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159148				0	lv	Select				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_DBFMT_FROM_USR\"\>Specifies a format from the list, if the format information of certain data fields is not accepted.\</ahelp\> The formats supplied here are only available for certain database fields, such as numeric or Boolean fields. If you select a database field in text format, you will not be able to select any format from the selection list, since the text format will be automatically maintained.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3144511				0	lv	If the format you want is not listed, select "Other Formats..." and define the desired format in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Number Format\"\>\<emph\>Number Format\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154282				0	lv	The number format assigned using the selection list always refers to the database field selected in the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	lv	To insert the data into the document in the form of a table, the correct \<emph\>Table\</emph\> option must be active. You can then select a database field from the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box to define the formatting of the database field. The changes to the number formats will be applied to the last selection. It does not matter whether the database field was selected from the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box or from the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	lv	Insert table heading				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150497				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:CB_TABLE_HEADON\"\>Specifies whether to insert a heading line for the columns in the text table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153178				0	lv	Apply column name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152922				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_HEADL_COLNMS\"\>Uses the field names of the database table as headings for each of the text table columns.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158407				0	lv	Create row only				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194	29			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_HEADL_EMPTY\"\>Inserts an empty heading line into the text table.\</ahelp\> Using the\<emph\> Create row only \</emph\>option, you can define headings in the document, which do not correspond to the database field names.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153369				0	lv	Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154299				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:PB_TBL_FORMAT\"\>Opens the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05090000.xhp\" name=\"Table Format\"\>\<emph\>Table Format\</emph\>\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Table Format\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> dialog, which enables you to define the table properties such as borders, background, and column width.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153728				0	lv	AutoFormat				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154988				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:PB_TBL_AUTOFMT\"\>Opens the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05150101.xhp\" name=\"AutoFormat\"\>\<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\>\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> dialog, in which you can select format styles that are immediately applied when inserting the table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Mail & News				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147102				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070200.xhp\" name=\"Mail News\"\>Mail & News\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Mail & News\</emph\> page in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> you can edit hyperlinks for e-mail or news addresses.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153528				0	lv	Mail & News				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153748				0	lv	E-mail				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_MAIL_RB_LINKTYP_MAIL\"\>Assigns the specified e-mail address to the hyperlink.\</ahelp\> Clicking the new hyperlink in the document will open a new message document, addressed to the receiver specified in the \<emph\>E-mail\</emph\> field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	lv	News				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149955				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_MAIL_RB_LINKTYP_NEWS\"\>Assigns a news address to the hyperlink.\</ahelp\> Clicking the hyperlink in the document will open a new message document to the news group you entered in the \<emph\>Receiver\</emph\> field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149580				0	lv	Receiver				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HYPERDLG_MAIL_PATH\"\>Specifies the full URL of the addressee, in the form mailto:name@provider.com or news:group.server.com.\</ahelp\> You can also use drag-and-drop.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143270				0	lv	Data Sources				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_IMAGEBUTTON_RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_MAIL_BTN_ADRESSBOOK\"\>Hides or shows the data source browser.\</ahelp\> Drag the receiver's \<emph\>E-mail\</emph\> data field from the data source browser into the \<emph\>Receiver\</emph\> text field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153332				0	lv	Subject				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_EDIT_RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_MAIL_ED_SUBJECT\"\>Specifies the subject that is inserted in the subject line of the new message document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
