helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151299				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/18010000.xhp\" name=\"Selection\"\>Selection\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148520				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SelectObject\"\>Allows you to select objects in the current document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149511				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3159194\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159194\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	lv	Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	lv	To select an object, click the object with the arrow. To select more than one object, drag a selection frame around the objects. To add an object to a selection, press Shift, and then click the object. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>The objects selected together can then be defined as a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05290000.xhp\" name=\"group\"\>group\</link\>, turning them into a single group object.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>You can edit individual elements of a group. You can also delete elements from a group with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Shift\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+click.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>You can select single objects from a group by double-clicking, if you first disable the \<emph\>Double-click to edit Text\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Option\</emph\> Bar.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Special Tips for Table Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109850				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>table controls; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of table controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table controls;keyboard-only edit mode\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850				0	lv	Special Tips for Table Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	lv	You can define a table control to display the records as you like. In other words you can define data fields for displaying or editing data like in a database form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152372				0	lv	The following fields are possible in a table control: text, date, time and currency field, numeric field, pattern field, check box and combo box. In the case of combined date/time fields, two columns are created automatically.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194				0	lv	The number of selected lines, if any are selected, is in parentheses after the total number of records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155616				0	lv	To insert columns into the table control, click in the column heads and bring up the context menu. The following commands are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	lv	Insert Column				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_INSERTCOL\"\>Calls a submenu to select a data field to adopt it in the table control.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	lv	Configure the table control using drag and drop: Open the data source browser and drag the desired fields out of the data source browser and on to the column heads of the table control. A pre-configured column is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827				0	lv	Replace with				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_CHANGECOL\"\>Opens a submenu to select a data field to replace the data field selected in the table control.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	lv	Delete Column				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETECOL\"\>Deletes the currently selected column.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	lv	Column				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	lv	Opens the properties dialog of the selected column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148539				0	lv	Hide Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_HIDECOL\"\>Hides the selected column.\</ahelp\> Its properties are not changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771				0	lv	Show columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS\"\>Calls a submenu where you can select the columns to show again.\</ahelp\> To show only one column, click the column name. You see only the first 16 hidden columns. If there are more hidden columns, choose the \<emph\>More\</emph\> command to call the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193				0	lv	More				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159269				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS_MORE\"\>Calls the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVX_DLG_SHOWGRIDCOLUMNS:1\"\>In the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog you can select the columns to be shown. Hold down the Shift or Ctrl (Mac: Command) key to select multiple entries.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561				0	lv	All				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	87			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWALLCOLS\"\>Click \<emph\>All \</emph\>if you want to show all columns.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153349				0	lv	Keyboard-only control of Table Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149416				0	lv	If you use the keyboard only to travel through controls in your document, you will find one difference to the other types of controls: the Tab key does not move the cursor to the next control, but moves to the next column inside the table control. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the next control, or press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the previous control.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153062				0	lv	To enter the special keyboard-only edit mode for Table Controls:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	lv	The form document must be in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"design mode\"\>design mode\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	lv	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to select the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3161657				0	lv	Press Shift+F4 to select the first control. If the Table Control is not the first control, press Tab until it is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	lv	Press Enter to enter the edit mode. The handles are shown farther out from the control border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	lv	In the edit mode, you can open the edit mode context menu by pressing Shift+F10.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	lv	If you want to edit columns, press Shift+Space to enter column edit mode. Now you can rearrange the order of columns with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow keys. The Delete key deletes the current column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	lv	Press the Escape key to exit the edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Standard Filter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151097				0	lv	Standard Filter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataFilterStandardFilter\"\>Specifies the logical conditions to filter your table data.\</ahelp\> This dialog is available for spreadsheet documents, database tables and database forms. The dialog for databases does not contain the \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EE				0	lv	         \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp#filters\"/\>      				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155555				0	lv	Filter criteria				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834				0	lv	You can define a filter by indicating the type of line, the name of the field, a logical condition and a value or a combination of arguments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149751				0	lv	Operator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_FILTERCRIT_LB_WHERECOND3\"\>For the following arguments, you can choose between the logical operators AND / OR.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149182				0	lv	Field name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_FILTERCRIT_LB_WHEREFIELD3\"\>Specifies the field names from the current table to set them in the argument.\</ahelp\> You will see the column identifiers if no text is available for the field names.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	lv	Condition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150254				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_FILTERCRIT_LB_WHERECOMP3\"\>Specifies the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12090101.xhp\" name=\"comparative operators\"\>comparative operators\</link\> through which the entries in the \<emph\>Field name\</emph\> and \<emph\>Value\</emph\> fields can be linked.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149166				0	lv	Value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149795				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_EDIT_DLG_FILTERCRIT_ET_WHEREVALUE3\"\>Specifies a value to filter the field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150976	14			0	lv	The\<emph\> Value \</emph\>list box contains all possible values for the specified \<emph\>Field name\</emph\> . Choose the value to be used in the filter. You can also choose the \<emph\>- empty -\</emph\> or \<emph\>-not empty -\</emph\> entries..				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156118	15			0	lv	If you use the filter function in database tables or forms, then type the value in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>text box to be used for filtering.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040201.xhp\" name=\"More Options\"\>More Options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\fontwork.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Fontwork Gallery				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10557				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/fontwork.xhp\"\>Fontwork Gallery\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10567				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The icon opens the Fontwork Gallery from which you can insert graphical text art into your document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10591				0	lv	Fontwork Gallery				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10595				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Fontwork Gallery displays previews of Fontwork objects. To insert an object into your document, select the object, and then click OK.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AF				0	lv	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/fontwork.xhp#fontwork\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10623				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/fontwork_toolbar.xhp\"\>Fontwork toolbar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
