helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id2439039				0	lv	Sets another environment for the program start.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id2789086				0	lv	Use soffice -env:UserInstallation=$(URL) where $(URL) is the URL of a folder that contains the "user" folder.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	lv	-p {filename1} {filename2} ...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3163666				0	lv	Prints the files \<emph\>{filename1} {filename2} ...\</emph\> to the default printer and ends. The splash screen does not appear.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150828				0	lv	If the file name contains spaces, then it must be enclosed in quotation marks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	lv	-pt {Printername} {filename1} {filename2} ...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155081				0	lv	Prints the files \<emph\>{filename1} {filename2} ...\</emph\> to the printer \<emph\>{Printername}\</emph\> and ends. The splash screen does not appear.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153655				0	lv	If the file name contains spaces, then it must be enclosed in quotation marks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154372				0	lv	-o {filename}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150309				0	lv	Opens \<emph\>{filename}\</emph\> for editing, even if it is a template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182				0	lv	-view {filename}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	lv	Creates a temporary copy of \<emph\>{filename}\</emph\> and opens it read-only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3166421				0	lv	-n {filename}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154259				0	lv	Creates a new document using \<emph\>{filename}\</emph\> as a template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155126				0	lv	-nologo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151334				0	lv	Disables the splash screen at program start.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	lv	-nodefault				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153306				0	lv	Starts without displaying anything except the splash screen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id2211676				0	lv	-nofirststartwizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id1641895				0	lv	Add this parameter to the program start command to suppress the Welcome Wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	lv	-display {display}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146786	46			0	lv	Sets the \<emph\>DISPLAY \</emph\>environment variable on UNIX based platforms to the value \<emph\>{display}\</emph\>. This parameter is only supported by the start script for the $[officename] software on UNIX based platforms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149595				0	lv	-headless				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150530				0	lv	Starts in "headless mode" which allows using the application without user interface.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156353				0	lv	This special mode can be used when the application is controlled by external clients via the \<link href=\"https://api.openoffice.org\" name=\"API\"\>API\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Printing in Black and White				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150125				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>printing; black and white\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>black and white printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colors; not printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; printing in black\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150125				0	lv	\<variable id=\"print_blackwhite\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/print_blackwhite.xhp\" name=\"Printing in Black and White\"\>Printing in Black and White\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	lv	Printing text and graphics in black and white				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. The \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page of the dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	lv	Click on \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. This opens the Properties dialog for your printer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	lv	Select the option to print in black and white. For further information, refer to the user's manual of your printer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	lv	Confirm the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog and click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	lv	The current document will be printed in black and white.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	lv	Printing in black and white in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	lv	Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress or Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Draw, as appropriate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	lv	Then choose \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573	12			0	lv	Under \<emph\>Quality,\</emph\> select either \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> or \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307				0	lv	When either of these options is selected, all presentations or drawings will be printed without color. If you only want to print in black for the \<emph\>current\</emph\> print job, select the option in \<emph\>File - Print - %PRODUCTNAME Draw/Impress\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149786	15			0	lv	               \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> converts all colors to a maximum of 256 gradations from black to white. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610	16			0	lv	               \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> converts all colors into the two values black and white. All borders around objects are printed black. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	lv	Printing only text in black and white				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	lv	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer you can choose to print color-formatted text in black and white. You can specify this either for all subsequent text documents to be printed, or only for the current printing process.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150358				0	lv	Printing all text documents with black and white text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	lv	Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer or Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer/Web.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	lv	Then choose \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910	22			0	lv	Under \<emph\>Contents,\</emph\> mark \<emph\>Print black\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	lv	All text documents or HTML documents will be printed with black text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148920				0	lv	Printing the current text document with black and white text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. Then click the \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Print text in black\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\" name=\"Printing dialogs\"\>Printing dialogs\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154146				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options dialog\"\>Tools - Options dialog\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying areas to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; sheet areas, to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;sheet areas in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	lv	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_table.xhp\" name=\"Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\"\>Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	lv	Open both the text document and the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	lv	Select the sheet area you want to copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	lv	Point to the selected area and press the mouse button. Keep the mouse button pressed for a moment, then drag the area into the text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	32			0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible next to each other, first drag the mouse pointer to the destination document button. Continue to hold down the mouse button. The document is displayed, and you can move the mouse pointer within the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	lv	Once the cursor is located in the place where you want to insert the sheet area, release the mouse button. The sheet area is inserted as an OLE object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	lv	You can select and edit the OLE object at any time.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	lv	To edit the OLE object, double-click on it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155389				0	lv	Alternatively, select the object and choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Edit\</emph\> or choose \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> from the context menu. You edit the object in its own frame within the text document, but you see the icons and menu commands needed for spreadsheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to open the source document of the OLE object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Changing Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154285				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>modifying, see changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing, see also editing and replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default templates; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;editing and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;templates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154285				0	lv	\<variable id=\"standard_template\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/standard_template.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Templates\"\>Changing Default Templates\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	lv	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customized Styles or other contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	lv	Modifying Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	lv	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	lv	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	lv	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	lv	Double-click \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> in the list on the left. You will see the user-defined templates in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>. Select the template you have just saved and open the context menu or open the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947				0	lv	Resetting Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	lv	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	lv	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	lv	Using Custom Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	lv	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109				0	lv	Templates in the Template Folder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	lv	You can save a new template with \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> or by selecting "Template" file type in any Save dialog. Save the template in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\> to be able to access the template from within the \<emph\>File - New - From Templates and Documents\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	lv	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialog before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	lv	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147315				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Templates\"\>Templates\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Assistive Tools in $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] assistive technology\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assistive technology in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen readers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	lv	\<variable id=\"assistive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"Assistive Tools in $[officename]\"\>Assistive Tools in $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	lv	$[officename] supports some assistive technology tools like screen magnification software, screen readers, and on-screen keyboards. Most of these tools communicate with $[officename] by means of the Java(TM) Access Bridge software, that uses the Java Accessibility API, a part of the Java runtime environment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id8847010				0	lv	A current list of supported assistive tools can be found on the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Accessibility\"\>Apache OpenOffice Wiki\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	lv	Requirements to use assistive tools in $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	lv	Java Runtime Environment (JRE) version 1.4.1_01 and higher, or version 1.4.0_02 with the locale set to "en_us".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	lv	Most recent version of the software for your assistive tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	15			0	lv	On Windows systems, \<link href=\"http://www.sun.com/access/downloads/\" name=\"Java Access Bridge\"\>Java Access Bridge\</link\> software version 1.0.3 or higher 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	lv	On UNIX(R) systems, the GNOME 2 desktop environment with the Java Access Bridge software for GNOME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149795				0	lv	Supported Assistive Tools				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	lv	On Windows systems, $[officename] directly supports most on-screen keyboard software. Additional support for assistive tools is provided by the Java Access Bridge software. The following is a list of some assistive tools that use the Java Access Bridge software to exchange data with $[officename]:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	lv	ZoomText Screen Magnifier (version 7.11 or higher)(Windows)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	lv	Gnopernicus Screen Reader and Magnifier, using GNOME Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface (at-spi) and Java Accessibility API software				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	lv	GNOME On Screen Keyboard (GOK), using GNOME at-spi and Java Accessibility API software				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061				0	lv	Supported Input Devices				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	lv	$[officename] provides the ability to use alternative input devices for access to all functions of $[officename].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045				0	lv	Screen magnification software allow users with low vision to work in $[officename] with caret and focus tracking.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	lv	On-screen keyboards enable users to perform almost all data input and commands with a mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	lv	Screen readers allow visually impaired users to access $[officename] with text-to-speech and Braille displays.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149808				0	lv	When accessibility support in $[officename] is enabled, the Java Runtime Environment is loaded, and increases the startup time for $[officename].				20200411 15:09:53
