helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	lv	In the Help window, you can show or hide the navigation pane as needed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3156411				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3153345\" src=\"sfx2/res/indexon_small.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153345\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	lv	On the toolbar of the \<emph\>Help\</emph\> window, click the left icon to show or hide the navigation pane.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Viewing File Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152594				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>properties;files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files;properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;file properties\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152594				0	lv	\<variable id=\"viewing_file_properties\"\>\<variable id=\"viewing\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/viewing_file_properties.xhp\" name=\"Viewing File Properties\"\>Viewing File Properties\</link\>\</variable\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	lv	File properties, such as author name, subject, and keywords, help you manage and identify your documents. $[officename] also tracks file statistics, including the number of words and the number of pages in a document, and automatically adds the statistics as part of the file property.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834				0	lv	You can view file properties for the current document\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\> or for a document in the Windows File Open dialog \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233				0	lv	To view file properties for the current document:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3153311				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150443				0	lv	To view file properties for a document listed in the Windows File Open dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	lv	Select a file in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	lv	Right-click and choose\<emph\> Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Table Design				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155448				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; creating in design view (manually)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>designing; database tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>properties;fields in databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fields;database tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoValue (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>primary keys;design view\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	lv	\<variable id=\"data_tabledefine\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\" name=\"Table Design\"\>Table Design\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	lv	This section contains information about how to create a new database table in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05010000.xhp\" name=\"design view\"\>design view\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288				0	lv	Open the database file of the database where you want a new table. Click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon. Choose \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\> to create a new table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798				0	lv	In the Design view, you can now create the fields for your table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349				0	lv	Enter new fields in rows from top to bottom. Click the \<emph\>Field Name\</emph\> cell and enter a field name for each data field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id1595507				0	lv	Include a "primary key" data field. Base needs a primary key to be able to edit the table contents. A primary key has unique contents for each data record. For example, insert a numerical field, right-click the first column, and choose \<emph\>Primary Key\</emph\> from the context menu. Set \<emph\>AutoValue\</emph\> to "Yes", so Base can automatically increment the value for each new record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	lv	In the next cell to the right, define the \<emph\>Field Type\</emph\>. When you click in the cell, you can select a field type in the combo box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	lv	Each field can only accept data corresponding to the specified field type. For example, it is not possible to enter text in a number field. Memo fields in dBASE III format are references to internally-managed text files which can hold up to 64KB text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	lv	You can enter an optional \<emph\>Description\</emph\> for each field. The text of the description will appear as a tip on the column headings in the table view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	lv	Field Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	lv	Enter properties for each selected data field. Depending on the database type, some input facilities may not be available.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> box, enter the default contents for every new record. This contents can be edited later.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Entry required\</emph\> box, specify whether or not the field may remain empty.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	lv	For the \<emph\>Length\</emph\> box, a combo box may be shown that provides the available choices.				20200411 15:09:53
