helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	lv	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1110200810120034				0	lv	In Writer text documents you can also accept or reject changes by choosing commands from the context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	lv	When you edit a document in which others have made changes, you can accept or reject the changes individually or all together.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	lv	If you have put multiple copies of the document in circulation, first merge these into one document (see \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp#redlining_docmerge\"/\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	lv	Open the document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Accept or Reject\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	lv	Select a change on the \<emph\>List\</emph\> tab. The change is selected and displayed in the document and you can now enter your decision with one of the buttons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	lv	If one author has modified another author's change, you will see the changes hierarchically arranged with a plus sign for opening up the hierarchy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	lv	If the list of changes is too long, you can switch to the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> tab in the dialog and specify that you only want to see the changes of certain authors, or only the changes of the last day, or that you want the list to be restricted in some other way.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	lv	Color-coded entries display the result of the filter that is set. Entries in black can be accepted or rejected and match the filter criteria. Entries in blue do not themselves match the filter criteria, but have subentries that are included by the filter. Gray entries cannot be accepted or rejected and do not match the filter criterion. Green entries do match the filter but cannot be accepted or rejected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Navigator for Document Overview				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147008				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>documents; contents as lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Navigator; contents as lists\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147008				0	lv	\<variable id=\"navigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/navigator.xhp\" name=\"Navigator for Document Overview\"\>Navigator for Document Overview\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	lv	All contents of the Navigator window are referred to here as "categories," whether titles, sheets, tables, text frames, graphics, OLE objects, sections, hyperlinks, references, indexes or comments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3153662				0	lv	The Navigator displays all types of objects contained in a document. If a plus sign appears next to a category, this indicates that at least one object of this kind exists. If you rest the mouse pointer on the category name, the number of objects is displayed in an extended tip.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	lv	Open a category by clicking on the plus sign. If you only want to view the entries in a certain category, select the category and click the \<emph\>Content View\</emph\> icon. Until you click the icon again, only the objects of this category will be displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3166461				0	lv	You may dock the Navigator to any document border or turn it back into a free window (double click on the gray area). You can change the size of the Navigator when it is a free window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Saving Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147226				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>documents; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backups; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>FTP; saving documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147226				0	lv	\<variable id=\"doc_save\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_save.xhp\" name=\"Saving Documents\"\>Saving Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> icon or press the shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+S.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3152349\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_save.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152349\"\>This icon is for tips on how to use the program more effectively.\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	lv	The document is saved under its path and name on the current local data medium or network drive or on the Internet, overwriting any file of the same name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	lv	When you save a new file for the first time, the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>Save As\</link\> dialog opens, in which you can enter a name, folder and drive or volume for the file. To open this dialog, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	lv	You can set the automatic creation of a backup copy under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	hd_id7146824				0	lv	Automatic extension to the file name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id9359111				0	lv	When saving a file, %PRODUCTNAME always appends an extension to the file name, except when the file name already has an extension that matches the file type. See the list of \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>ODF extensions\</link\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id6709494				0	lv	Some examples for the automatic extensions are listed in the following table:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id9009674				0	lv	You enter this file name				20200411 15:09:53
