helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id1022200911011975				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The Open icon presents a file open dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id082020080310500				0	lv	The \<emph\>Open\</emph\> icon presents a \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_open.xhp\"\>file open\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Registering and Deleting a Database 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	bm_id4724570				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>databases;registering (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;registered databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	lv	\<variable id=\"data_register\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_register.xhp\"\>Registering and Deleting a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	lv	Data from any \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> can be registered to %PRODUCTNAME. To register means to tell %PRODUCTNAME where the data is located, how it is organized, how to get that data, and more. Once the database is registered, you can use the menu command \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to access the data records from your text documents and spreadsheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	lv	To register an existing database file:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	lv	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E1				0	lv	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and select the database file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	lv	To remove a registered database from %PRODUCTNAME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	lv	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10719				0	lv	Select the database file and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F3				0	lv	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FB				0	lv	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Inserting Hyperlinks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	lv	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	lv	You can insert hyperlinks in two ways: as text or as a button. In both cases, the visible text can be different from the URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	7			0	lv	Display the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>. Type the visible text in the left field and the full URL in the right field, including http:// or file://.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	8			0	lv	Place the text cursor in the document at the point where you want to insert the hyperlink. Click the\<emph\> Hyperlink\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\>. The hyperlink is inserted as text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	lv	If you want to insert the hyperlink as a button, click and hold the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>As Button\</emph\> from the sub-menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3149763\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_hyperlinkdialog.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149763\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	30			0	lv	To use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> instead of the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> to define the hyperlink, click the icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	23			0	lv	To jump to a specific line in a text document, first enter a bookmark at that position (\<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>). 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076D				0	lv	To jump to a cell in a spreadsheet, first enter a name for the cell (\<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	lv	In the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> combo box, enter only the short form of the URL when jumping within the same document: If the bookmark is called \<emph\>Target\</emph\>, enter \<emph\>Target\</emph\>. To jump to another document, enter the complete URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152887				0	lv	Hyperlinks can also be inserted by drag-and-drop from the Navigator. Hyperlinks can refer to references, headings, graphics, tables, objects, directories or bookmarks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	lv	If you wish to insert in a text a hyperlink that refers to Table 1, drag the entry Table 1 from the Navigator and drop it in the text. To do this, the \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink\</emph\> drag mode must be selected in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153394				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; copying between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394				0	lv	\<variable id=\"copy_drawfunctions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copy_drawfunctions.xhp\" name=\"Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\"\>Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	28			0	lv	In $[officename] it is possible to copy drawing objects between text, spreadsheets and presentation documents. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	lv	Select the drawing object or objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	lv	Copy the drawing object to the clipboard, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	lv	Switch to the other document and place the cursor where the drawing object is to be inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	lv	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573				0	lv	Inserting into a text document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	lv	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current paragraph. You can change the anchor by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar. This opens a popup menu where you can select the anchor type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	lv	Inserting into a spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	30			0	lv	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current cell. You can change the anchor between cell and page by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149456\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleanchortype.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149456\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Configuring $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>configuring; $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customizing; $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	lv	\<variable id=\"configure_overview\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/configure_overview.xhp\" name=\"Configuring $[officename]\"\>Configuring $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	lv	You can customize your $[officename] to suit your needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	lv	Use \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Customize\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Customize\</emph\> dialog to change toolbars, menus and other user interface items.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3145071				0	lv	You are free to change the items on the menu bar. You can delete items, add new ones, copy items from one menu to another, rename them, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	lv	The toolbars may be freely configured.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	lv	You can change the shortcut keys.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3153345				0	lv	You can change default settings of $[officename] to suit your needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	optid3155421				0	lv	Use \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/010000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> dialog to change a variety of settings you will use in $[officename] modules. Items presented in the \<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\> menu will change depending on the module you are using.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3145071				0	lv	In \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/language_select.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - Language Settings\</emph\>\</link\>, you will find options for your default language and currency setting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3149811				0	lv	In \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] Writer - Basic Fonts\</emph\>\</link\>, you will find default font settings. Change these to suit your preferences. Fonts can easily be changed on per document basis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3150443				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010900.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - Print\</emph\>\</link\> contains a number of print customizations that may be useful for your particular needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Customize\"\>Tools - Customize\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3155388				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options\"\>Tools - Options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>ImageMap; editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editors; ImageMap editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>images; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hotspots;adding to images\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>URL;in pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10631				0	lv	\<variable id=\"imagemap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/imagemap.xhp\"\>Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	lv	An ImageMap allows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a picture in your document. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	lv	You can draw three types of hotspots: rectangles, ellipses, and polygons. When you click a hotspot, the URL is opened in the browser window or frame that you specify. You can also specify the text that appears when your mouse rests on the hotspot.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10677				0	lv	To add a clickable hotspot to an image				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	lv	Position the cursor where you want the ImageMap in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>, select and insert a bitmap picture.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	lv	With the picture selected, choose \<emph\>Edit - ImageMap\</emph\>. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>, which displays the picture at the background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	lv	Use the icons in the ImageMap Editor to draw a hotspot shape, for example a rectangle, over the image at the background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	lv	You can see an extended help text on the functions of each icon when you enable Extended Help in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	lv	Enter the "Address" URL that will be shown in a Web browser when the user clicks the hotspot.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	lv	Optionally, enter the "Text" that will be shown as a tip when the user points the mouse to the hotspot.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B3				0	lv	Click the Apply button to apply your changes, and close the ImageMap Editor.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	lv	Save the document in the %PRODUCTNAME or HTML format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	lv	You may save the ImageMap as a file and upload that file to a Web server, for example.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Turning Extended Tips On and Off				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156414				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>Help; extended tips on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extended tips in Help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tips;extended tips in Help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tooltips;extended tips\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>activating;extended help tips\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156414				0	lv	\<variable id=\"active_help_on_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/active_help_on_off.xhp\" name=\"Turning Extended Tips On and Off\"\>Turning Extended Tips On and Off\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	lv	\<emph\>Extended tips\</emph\> provide a brief description of the function of a particular icon, text box or menu command when you rest your cursor on that item.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155339				0	lv	To turn Extended Tips on and off:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>, and check \<emph\>Extended tips\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	lv	A check mark indicates that the extended tips are activated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	lv	To turn Extended Tips on temporarily:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	lv	Press the shortcut keys Shift+F1 to activate extended tips once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	lv	A question mark appears beside the mouse pointer. You can move this \<emph\>Help Mouse Pointer\</emph\> over all controls, icons and menu commands to obtain a description of the command. The \<emph\>Help Mouse Pointer\</emph\> is disabled the next time you click the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Inserting and Editing Buttons				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149798				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>command buttons, see push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>controls;adding to documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keys;adding push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>buttons;adding push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>press buttons, see push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>push buttons;adding to documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	lv	\<variable id=\"formfields\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/formfields.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Buttons\"\>Adding a Command Button to a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	lv	You can use the Form Controls toolbar to add checkboxes, buttons, tables showing data records, and other controls to a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077F				0	lv	To Add a Button to a Document 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	lv	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A4				0	lv	The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	lv	In the document, drag to draw the button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	lv	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CD				0	lv	Specify the properties of the button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	lv	To change the button label, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and edit the text in the \<emph\>Label\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303	12			0	lv	To attach a macro to the button, click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab, and click the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button beside the button action that you want to run the macro. In the \<emph\>Assign Macro\</emph\> dialog, locate the macro that you want to use, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10814				0	lv	Close the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147350				0	lv	(Optional) Specify the properties of the form that the button belongs to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	lv	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Form\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	lv	The \<emph\>Form Properties\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	lv	Specify the properties for the form and then close the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155805				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>tables in text; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in spreadsheets;defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; for tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; around tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;table borders\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155805				0	lv	\<variable id=\"border_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/border_table.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\"\>Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147008				0	lv	Setting a Predefined Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	lv	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	3			0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table \</emph\>toolbar (Writer) or on the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> bar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	lv	Click one of the predefined border styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	lv	This \<emph\>adds\</emph\> the selected style to the current border style of the table cells. Select the blank border style at the top left of the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window to clear all border styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153666				0	lv	Setting a Customized Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	lv	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Table - Table Properties - Borders\</emph\> (Writer) or \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\> (Calc).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	lv	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id31594132				0	lv	If you select more than one row or column, you can change the middle lines between rows or columns. Select the middle markers in the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	lv	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	lv	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	lv	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	bm_id7430951				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>opening;documents on WebDAV server\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>digital signatures;WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	hd_id4989165				0	lv	\<variable id=\"digitalsign_receive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_receive.xhp\"\>Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	lv	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can open and save documents that are stored on a WebDAV server, using the secure HTTPS protocol.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	lv	You must use the %PRODUCTNAME file dialogs to use WebDAV over HTTPS.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	lv	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\>. Ensure that \<emph\>Use %PRODUCTNAME dialogs\</emph\> is enabled. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7424237				0	lv	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, enter the path to the WebDAV folder. For example, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>https://192.168.1.1/webfolder\</item\> to open a secure connection to the WebDAV server at the IP address 192.168.1.1, and to list the contents of the \<item type=\"literal\"\>webfolder\</item\> folder.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	lv	The first time you connect to a WebDAV server, you see the "\<emph\>Website Certified by an Unknown Authority\</emph\>" dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	lv	You should click the \<emph\>Examine Certificate\</emph\> button and examine the certificate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	lv	If you accept the certificate, choose "\<emph\>Accept this certificate temporarily for this session\</emph\>" and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. Now you can open and save files from the WebDAV server without further questions, until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	lv	If you do not trust the certificate, click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	lv	If you did accept the certificate, you can now select the file name or file names you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	lv	If there is a mismatch of the domain name given in the certificate and the domain name you entered in the file dialog, then you see a dialog that allows you to choose from any of the following options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	lv	 \<emph\>View Certificate\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the View Certificate dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	lv	 \<emph\>Continue\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you are sure both domains are the same, click the Continue button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9116794				0	lv	 \<emph\>Cancel Connection\</emph\> - Cancels the connection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	lv	If you click \<emph\>Continue\</emph\>, you may see a dialog that asks you to enter your user name and password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your user name to log on to the WebDAV server.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your password.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If you enable \<emph\>Remember password till end of session\</emph\>, your password will be remembered for subsequent WebDAV connections until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3204443				0	lv	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/How_to_use_digital_Signatures\"\>English Wiki page on digital signatures\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id2182378				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp\"\>About digital signatures\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Editing Graphic Objects 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145136				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>resizing, see also scaling/zooming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling, see also zooming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drawings, see also draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>graphic objects, see draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; drawing pictures\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; drawing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; copying when moving in presentations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects; adding/editing/copying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>circle drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>square drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>handles; scaling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling; objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects;moving and resizing with mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resizing;objects, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;scaling/resizing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145136				0	lv	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_drawit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_graphic_drawit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Graphic Objects\"\>Editing Graphic Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Drawing\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, if it is not already open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	lv	Drawing objects can be subsequently edited and modified. Drawing objects created in this way are vector graphics, which you can scale freely without any loss of quality.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	lv	To create a rectangle, click the rectangle icon and move your cursor to the place in the document where you want one corner of the rectangle to be. Press the mouse button and hold it down while dragging to the opposite corner of the rectangle. When you release the mouse button, the rectangle is inserted in the document. It is selected, and you can edit its properties through the context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>To draw multiple objects of the same type, double-click the icon.\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>To draw multiple objects of the same type, double-click the icon.\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Draw multiple objects of the same type. Click the document without moving the mouse to stop drawing objects.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	lv	If you want to open up draw objects from the center instead of dragging from one corner to the other, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while dragging. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>With some window managers, you may need to hold down also the meta key.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id9448225				0	lv	Holding down the Shift key while dragging restricts the created object. For example, instead of a rectangle you get a square, instead of an ellipse you get a circle. When you drag a handle of an existing object with Shift held down, the aspect ratio of the object is retained.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626				0	lv	To scale the objects, first select them by clicking on them with the selection tool. You then see eight handles around the object. When you drag one of the four corner handles, the opposite corner remains fixed while the other three corners move. When you drag one of the side handles, the opposite side remains fixed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id224616				0	lv	To scale a draw object using the keyboard, first select the object, then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab repeatedly to highlight one of the handles. Then press an arrow key. To scale in smaller steps, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while pressing an arrow key. Press Esc to leave the point edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	lv	To move draw objects, first select them. To select more than one object, press the Shift key while clicking. Select text objects by clicking exactly on their edge. While holding down the mouse button, drag the objects to the new location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id7199316				0	lv	To move a draw object using the keyboard, first select the object, then press an arrow key. To move in smaller steps, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while pressing an arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id7133399316				0	lv	To enter text to be a part of a graphics object, select the object and start typing your text. Click outside the object to end entering text. Double-click text inside an object to edit the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	lv	To revert to normal mode after creating and editing draw objects, click in an area of the document containing no objects. If you see a drawing cursor, first exit this mode by clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Information about the individual icons\"\>Information about the individual icons\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Fontwork For Graphical Text Art				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	bm_id3696707				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>graphical text art\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>designing; fonts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>TextArt, see Fontwork\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>WordArt, see Fontwork\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Fontwork\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text effects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>effects; Fontwork icons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; Fontwork icons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>3D text creation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rotating;3D text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;Fontwork objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;Fontwork objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066D				0	lv	\<variable id=\"fontwork\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/fontwork.xhp\"\>Fontwork For Graphical Text Art\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068B				0	lv	You can use Fontwork to create graphical text art objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10691				0	lv	To create a Fontwork object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_id0202200911373965				0	lv	If you don't see the Drawing toolbar or the Fontwork toolbar, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars\</item\> to enable the toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069C				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar or on the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Fontwork Gallery\</emph\> icon.\<image id=\"img_id7040009\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7040009\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_id3149761				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a Fontwork style and click OK to insert the Fontwork into your document. Double-click or Ctrl+double-click the Fontwork in your document to enter text edit mode and change the text.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Fontwork Gallery\</emph\> dialog, select a Fontwork style and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10755				0	lv	The Fontwork object is inserted into your document. Fontwork objects are Custom Shapes. Using the 3D Settings toolbar, you can switch the view at any time from 2D to 3D and back.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	lv	Double-click the object to enter text edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	lv	Replace the default Fontwork text with your own text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A8				0	lv	Press Esc to exit text edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AE				0	lv	To edit a Fontwork object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B5				0	lv	Click the Fontwork object. If the Fontwork object is inserted in the background, hold down the Ctrl key while you click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B8				0	lv	The \<link href=\"text/shared/fontwork_toolbar.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar is displayed. If you do not see the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> toolbar, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Fontwork\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BC				0	lv	Click an icon in the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10839				0	lv	The following icons are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	lv	Fontwork Gallery - adds another Fontwork object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C9				0	lv	Fontwork Shape - edits the shape				20200411 15:09:53
