helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id1413922				0	lv	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_create.xhp\"\>Creating XML Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053D				0	lv	Creating an XML Filter for %PRODUCTNAME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109A9				0	lv	When you create an XML filter for %PRODUCTNAME, you need to design an \<emph\>XSLT stylesheet\</emph\> that can convert to and from the OpenDocument XML file format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B0				0	lv	For more information about the OpenDocument XML format, go to \<link href=\"https://xml.openoffice.org/\"\>https://xml.openoffice.org/\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C5				0	lv	If you want, you can include a \<emph\>template\</emph\> with your filter to apply %PRODUCTNAME styles to an XML document that you import.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CC				0	lv	You can also include the \<emph\>Document Type Definition\</emph\> (DTD) for the external XML format so you can validate the XML format, for example, when you test the filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10531				0	lv	To Create an XML Filter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E0				0	lv	Create an XSLT transformation \<emph\>stylesheet\</emph\> that maps the elements of the external XML format to the elements of the OpenDocument XML file format and back again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E8				0	lv	Create a template that assigns %PRODUCTNAME styles to elements in the external XML format when you import a file in this format into %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	lv	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, create a text document, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109F4				0	lv	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109FC				0	lv	In the \<emph\>XML Filter\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and define the properties of the filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A03				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Filter Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the XML filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CA1				0	lv	This name is displayed in the \<emph\>XML Filter Settings\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A09				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Application\</emph\> box, select the %PRODUCTNAME application that the filter is for.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0F				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Name of File Type\</emph\> box, enter the file type that the filter is for.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	lv	This name is displayed in the list of file types in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\>, \<emph\>Export\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialogs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A15				0	lv	In the \<emph\>File extension\</emph\> box, enter the extension for the exported file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1B				0	lv	To differentiate the file from other XML files, enter an extension other than *.xml.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1F				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page, define the transformation properties for the filter.				20200411 15:09:53
