helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>labels; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>business cards; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>synchronizing;labels and business cards\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	lv	\<variable id=\"labels\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels.xhp\" name=\"Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\"\>Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	lv	Designing Business Cards Through a Dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798	70			0	lv	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Business Cards\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Business Cards\</emph\>\</link\> to open the\<emph\> Business Cards \</emph\>dialog, which allows you to choose how your business cards will look.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147654				0	lv	Designing Labels and Business Cards				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	lv	You can design both labels and business cards through the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	lv	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010200.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Labels\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, define the label format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	lv	$[officename] Writer contains many formats of commercially available sheets for labels, badges, and business cards. You can also add other, user-defined formats.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Inscription\</emph\>, you can choose what you want written on the labels.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	lv	This often involves database fields, so that the labels can be printed with varying content, when sending "Form Letters" for example. It is also possible to have the same text printed on every label.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	85			0	lv	Use the \<emph\>Database \</emph\>and \<emph\>Table \</emph\>list boxes to select the database and table from which the data fields are obtained. Click on the arrow button to transfer the selected data field into the inscription area. Press Enter to insert a line break. You can also enter spaces and any other fixed text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> tab you can define your own label formats, not covered by the predefined formats. To do this, select "User" from the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list box. On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, you can specify whether all labels or only certain ones are to be created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, make sure that the \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> box is selected. If this is selected, a label only has to be entered (on the top left label) and edited once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	lv	As soon as you click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, you will see a small window with the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button. Enter the first label. When you click on the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button, the current individual label is copied to all the other labels on the sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767				0	lv	Click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\> to create a new document with the settings you have entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Business Cards\"\>Business Cards\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Working With %PRODUCTNAME XML Filters 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>saving;to XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>loading;XML files\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>importing;from XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>exporting;to XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>file filters;XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XSLT filters, see also XML filters\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10923				0	lv	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter.xhp\"\>About XML Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10927				0	lv	%PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>stores documents in XML format\</link\>. You can create customized filters that convert the native OpenDocument XML file format used by %PRODUCTNAME into another format. These filters can be integrated into %PRODUCTNAME seamlessly so that you can save or load these formats transparently.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093A				0	lv	To create an XML filter, you must have a good understanding of XML and XSLT concepts. These concepts are beyond the scope of this help.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	lv	An XML filter contains \<emph\>stylesheets\</emph\> that are written in the XSLT language. The stylesheets define the transformation from the OpenDocument file format to another XML format through export and import filters. There are three types of XML filters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10947				0	lv	 \<emph\>Import Filters\</emph\> load external XML files and transform the format of the files into the OpenDocument XML file format. After you install an import filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10960				0	lv	 \<emph\>Export Filters\</emph\> transform OpenDocument XML files and \<emph\>save\</emph\> the files to a different XML format. After you install an export filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070001.xhp\"\>Export dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10979				0	lv	 \<emph\>Import/Export Filters\</emph\> load and save OpenDocument XML files into a different XML \<emph\>format\</emph\>. After you install these filters, the names of the filters are added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\> and the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\"\>File Save As dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B39				0	lv	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/Style/XSL/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible \<emph\>Stylesheet\</emph\> Language (XSL)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4E				0	lv	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/XML/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible Markup Language (XML)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D97				0	lv	 \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp#xmlformat\"/\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id5569017				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_distribute.xhp\"\>Distributing XML filters\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id6426892				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_create.xhp\"\>Creating and Testing XML filters\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
