helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150486				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"sw:CheckBox:TP_OPTPRINT_PAGE:CB_REVERSE\"\>Specifies whether to reverse the printing order. The last page of the document will then be the first one printed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147318				0	lv	Brochure				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417	24			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"sw:CheckBox:TP_OPTPRINT_PAGE:CB_PROSPECT\"\>Select the\<emph\> Brochure \</emph\>option to print your document in brochure format.\</ahelp\> The brochure format is as follows in $[officename] Writer:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149410				0	lv	If you print a document in portrait on a landscape page, two opposing sides in a brochure will be printed next to each other. If you have a printer with double-sided printing capability, you can create an entire brochure from your document without having to collate the pages later. If you have a printer that only has single-sided printing capability, you can achieve this effect by first printing the front pages with the "Front sides / right pages /odd pages" option marked, then re-inserting the entire paper stack in your printer and printing all the back pages with the "Back pages / left pages / even pages" option marked.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	hd_id9475386				0	lv	Right to left				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	par_id7894222				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Check to print the pages of the brochure in the correct order for a right-to-left script.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149300				0	lv	Comments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151320				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies whether comments in your document are printed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148916				0	lv	Other				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	hd_id4188055				0	lv	Print automatically inserted blank pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	par_id8295541				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If this option is enabled, automatically-inserted blank pages are being printed. This is best if you are printing double-sided. For example, in a book, a "chapter" paragraph style has been set to always start with an odd numbered page. If the previous chapter ends on an odd page, %PRODUCTNAME inserts an even numbered blank page. This option controls whether to print that even numbered page or not.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145642				0	lv	Create single print jobs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"sw:CheckBox:TP_OPTPRINT_PAGE:CB_SINGLEJOBS\"\>Specifies that each new print job will begin on a new page even if you are using a duplex printer.\</ahelp\> If this field is not checked then it is possible that the first page of the second copy is printed on the reverse side of the last page of the first copy, especially if there are an odd number of pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156384				0	lv	Paper tray from printer settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	par_id3146316				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"sw:CheckBox:TP_OPTPRINT_PAGE:CB_PAPERFROMSETUP\"\>For printers with multiple trays, the "Paper tray from printer settings" option specifies whether the paper tray used is specified by the system settings of the printer.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147362				0	lv	Fax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154703				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_OPTPRINT_PAGE:LB_FAX\"\>If you have installed fax software on your computer and wish to fax directly from the text document, select the desired fax machine.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Presentation Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155805				0	lv	%PRODUCTNAME Impress Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	lv	\<variable id=\"allgemein\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SdEditOptions\"\>Defines various settings for newly created presentation documents, such as the contents to be displayed, the measurement unit used, if and how grid alignment is carried out.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Calculate				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149399				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>references; iterative (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating;iterative references (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>iterative references in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>recursions in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>dates; default (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>dates; start 1900/01/01 (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>dates; start 1904/01/01 (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>case sensitivity;comparing cell contents (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>decimal places displayed (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>precision as shown (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>values; rounded as shown (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>rounding precision (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>search criteria for database functions in cells\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Excel; search criteria\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\" name=\"Calculate\"\>Calculate\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines the calculation settings for spreadsheets.\</ahelp\> Defines the behavior of spreadsheets with iterative references, the date settings, the number of decimal places, and if capitalization or lower cases are to be considered when searching within sheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149399				0	lv	Iterative references				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	lv	In this section you can delimit the number of approximation steps carried out during iterative calculations. In addition, you can specify the degree of precision of the answer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154142				0	lv	Iterations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149795	6			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_ITERATE\"\>Specifies whether formulas with iterative references (formulas that are continuously repeated until the problem is solved) are calculated after a specific number of repetitions.\</ahelp\> If the\<emph\> Iterations \</emph\>box is not marked, an iterative reference in the table will cause an error message.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148686	7			0	lv	         \<emph\>Example:\</emph\> calculating the cost of an item without the value-added tax.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	lv	Type the text 'Selling price' in cell A5, the text 'Net' in cell A6, and the text 'Value-added tax' in cell A7.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530	61			0	lv	Now type a selling price (for example, 100) in cell B5. The net price should be shown in cell B6 and the value-added tax should be shown in cell B7. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153061				0	lv	You know that the value-added tax is calculated as 'net price times 15%' and that you arrive at the net price by deducting the value-added tax from the selling price. Type the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=B5-B7\</item\> in B6 to calculate the net price, and type the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=B6*0.15\</item\> in cell B7 to calculate the value-added tax.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	lv	Switch on the iterations to correctly calculate the formulas, otherwise a 'Circular reference' error message appears in the \<emph\>Status\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	lv	A				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	lv	B				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149202				0	lv	5				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	lv	Selling Price				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	lv	100				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3159254				0	lv	6				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	lv	Net				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147348				0	lv	=B5-B7				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154918				0	lv	7				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153573				0	lv	Tax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	lv	=B6*0,15				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145750				0	lv	Steps				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:ED_STEPS\"\>Sets the maximum number of iteration steps.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153728				0	lv	Minimum Change				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153139				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:ED_EPS\"\>Specifies the difference between two consecutive iteration step results. If the result of the iteration is lower than the minimum change value, then the iteration will stop.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147125				0	lv	Date				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155416				0	lv	Select the start date for the internal conversion from days to numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147396				0	lv	12/30/1899 (default)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145646				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_DATESTD\"\>Sets 12/30/1899 as day zero.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156283				0	lv	01/01/1900 (StarCalc 1.0)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_DATESC10\"\>Sets 1/1/1900 as day zero. Use this setting for StarCalc 1.0 spreadsheets containing date entries.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156181				0	lv	01/01/1904				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153948				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_DATE1904\"\>Sets 1/1/1904 as day zero. Use this setting for spreadsheets that are imported in a foreign format.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153838				0	lv	Case sensitive				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146793				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_CASE\"\>Specifies whether to distinguish between upper and lower case in texts when comparing cell contents.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	28			0	lv	         \<emph\>Example:\</emph\> Type the text 'Test' in cell A1; and the text 'test' in B1. Then type the formula "=A1=B1" in cell C1. If the \<emph\>Case sensitive\</emph\> box is marked, FALSE will appear in the cell; otherwise, TRUE will appear in the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	lv	The EXACT text function is always case-sensitive, independent of the settings in this dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145231				0	lv	Decimal places				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:ED_PREC\"\>Defines the number of decimals to be displayed for numbers with the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> number format. The numbers are displayed as rounded numbers, but are not saved as rounded numbers.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145150				0	lv	Precision as shown				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150644				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_CALC\"\>Specifies whether to make calculations using the rounded values displayed in the sheet. Charts will be shown with the displayed values. If the \<emph\>Precision as shown\</emph\> option is not marked, the displayed numbers are rounded, but they are calculated internally using the non-rounded number.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152581				0	lv	Search criteria = and <> must apply to whole cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_MATCH\"\>Specifies that the search criteria you set for the Calc database functions must match the whole cell exactly. When the \<emph\>Search criteria = and <> must apply to whole cells\</emph\> box is marked, $[officename] Calc behaves exactly as MS Excel when searching cells in the database functions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148422				0	lv	.* in following position:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156139				0	lv	Search result:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150979				0	lv	win				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3159239				0	lv	Finds win, but not win95, os2win, or upwind				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153782				0	lv	win.*				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151278				0	lv	Finds win and win95, but not os2win or upwind				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155506				0	lv	.*win				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150886				0	lv	Finds win and os2win, but not win95 or upwind				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147167				0	lv	.*win.*				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	lv	Finds win, win95, os2win, and upwind				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148814	44			0	lv	If \<emph\>Search criteria = and <> must apply to whole cells \</emph\>is not enabled, the "win" search pattern acts like ".*win.*". The search pattern can be at any position within the cell when searching with the Calc database functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156448				0	lv	Enable regular expressions in formulas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155092				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CALC_BTN_REGEX\"\>Specifies that regular expressions are enabled when searching and also for character string comparisons.\</ahelp\>\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\> This relates to the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060101.xhp\" name=\"database functions\"\>database functions\</link\>, and to VLOOKUP, HLOOKUP and SEARCH.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156199				0	lv	Automatically find column and row labels				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_LOOKUP\"\>Specifies that you can use the text in any cell as a label for the column below the text or the row to the right of the text. The text must consist of at least one word and must not contain any operators.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242	57			0	lv	         \<emph\>Example\</emph\>: Cell E5 contains the text "Europe". Below, in cell E6, is the value 100 and in cell E7 the value 200. If the \<emph\>Automatically find column and row labels\</emph\> box is marked, you can write the following formula in cell A1: =SUM(Europe).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id315634199				0	lv	Limit decimals for general number format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id315343818				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>You can specify the maximum number of decimal places that are shown by default for cells with General number format. If not enabled, cells with General number format show as many decimal places as the column width allows.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Compatibility				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3577990				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>Word documents;compatibility\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;compatibility settings for text import\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>options;compatibility (Writer)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>compatibility settings for MS Word import\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Office;importing Word documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>layout;importing Word documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;printer metrics (Writer)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>metrics;document formatting (Writer)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printer metrics for document formatting (Writer)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10607				0	lv	\<variable id=\"compatibility_var\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01041000.xhp\"\>Compatibility\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10625				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"53251\"\>Specifies compatibility settings for text documents. These options help in fine-tuning %PRODUCTNAME when importing Microsoft Word documents.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	lv	Some of the settings defined here are only valid for the current document and must be defined separately for each document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400				0	lv	Use printer metrics for document formatting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE_CB_PRINTER_METRICS\"\>Specifies that printer metrics are applied for printing and also for formatting the display on the screen.\</ahelp\> If this box is not checked, a printer independent layout will be used for screen display and printing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155768				0	lv	If you set this option for the current document and then save the document, for example, in an older binary format, this option will not be saved. If you later open the file from the older format, this option will be set by default.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145640				0	lv	Add spacing between paragraphs and tables (in current document)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	lv	In $[officename] Writer, paragraph spacing is defined differently than in MS Word documents. If you have defined spacing between two paragraphs or tables, spacing is also added in the corresponding MS Word documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE:CB_MERGE_PARA_DIST\"\>Specifies whether to add MS Word-compatible spacing between paragraphs and tables in $[officename] Writer text documents.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	lv	Add paragraph and table spacing at tops of pages (in current document)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE:CB_MERGE_PARA_DIST_PAGESTART\"\>Specifies whether paragraph spacing at the top of a page will also be effective at the beginning of a page or column if the paragraph is positioned on the first page of the document.\</ahelp\> The same applies for a page break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145789				0	lv	If you import an MS Word document, the spaces are automatically added during the conversion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149964				0	lv	Use %WRITERCOMPATIBILITYVERSIONOOO11 tab stop formatting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152777				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE_CB_TAB_ALIGNMENT\"\>Specifies how to align text at tab stops beyond the right margin, how to handle decimal tab stops, and how to handle tab stops close to a line break.\</ahelp\> If this check box is not selected, tab stops are handled in the same way as in other Office applications.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10810				0	lv	In text documents created by your current version of Writer, the new tab stop handling is used by default. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the old tab stop handling is applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	lv	Do not add leading (extra space) between lines of text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10806				0	lv	Specifies that additional leading (extra space) between lines of text is not added, even if the font in use contains the additional leading attribute.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	lv	In text documents created by your current version of Writer, the additional leading is used by default. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the additional leading is not used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FF				0	lv	Use %WRITERCOMPATIBILITYVERSIONOOO11 line spacing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10815				0	lv	If the option is off, a new process for formatting text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied. If the option is on, the previous method of formatting of text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10818				0	lv	In text documents created by your current version of Writer and in Microsoft Word documents of recent versions, the new process is used. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the previous process is used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	lv	Add paragraph and table spacing at bottom of table cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	lv	Specifies that the bottom spacing is added to a paragraph, even when it is the last paragraph in a table cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10849				0	lv	If the option is off, table cells will be formatted as in Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0. If the option is on, an alternative method of formatting table cells will be applied. The option is on by default for new documents created with %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION and for documents imported from Microsoft Word format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084C				0	lv	Use %WRITERCOMPATIBILITYVERSIONOOO11 object positioning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10864				0	lv	Specifies how to calculate the position of floating objects anchored to a character or paragraph with respect to the top and bottom paragraph spacing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10867				0	lv	If the option is on, the floating objects are positioned as in Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0. If the option is off, the floating objects are positioned using an alternative method that is similar to the method used by Microsoft Word. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1086A				0	lv	The option will be set to off for new documents. For Writer documents created by a version prior to %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION the option is on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10821				0	lv	Use %WRITERCOMPATIBILITYVERSIONOOO11 text wrapping around objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id4016541				0	lv	MS Word and Writer have different approaches on wrapping text around floating screen objects. Floating screen object are Writer frames and drawing objects, and the objects 'text box', 'graphic', 'frame', 'picture' etc. in MS Word.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id7280190				0	lv	In MS Word and in current versions of Writer, page header/footer content and footnote/endnote content does not wrap around floating screen objects. Text body content wraps around floating screen objects which are anchored in the page header. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id2782982				0	lv	In Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the opposite was true.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10892				0	lv	If the option is off, which is the default setting, the new text wrapping will be applied. If the option is on, the former text wrapping will be applied. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092A				0	lv	Consider wrapping style when positioning objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	lv	Specifies how the complex process of positioning floating objects that are anchored to a character or paragraph should work. In Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, an iterative process was used, while in current versions a straightforward process is used, which is similar to the same process in Microsoft Word.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10943				0	lv	If the option is off, the old %PRODUCTNAME iterative process of object positioning is used. If the option is on, the new straightforward process is used to ensure compatibility with Microsoft Word documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5240028				0	lv	Expand word space on lines with manual line breaks in justified paragraphs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id8599810				0	lv	If enabled, Writer adds spacing between words, in lines that end with Shift+Enter in justified paragraphs. If disabled, spacing between words will not be expanded to justify the lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id8012634				0	lv	This setting is on by default for .odt text documents. It will be saved and loaded with the document in the .odt text document format. This setting cannot be saved in old .sxw text documents, so this setting is off for .sxw text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10845				0	lv	Use as Default				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10848				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"879350288\"\>Click to use the current settings on this tab page as the default for further sessions with %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
