helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666				0	lv	The following settings are \<emph\>always\</emph\> loaded with a document, whether or not this option is marked:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148946				0	lv	Data source linked to the document and its view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id927152				0	lv	Load printer settings with the document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id5684987				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If enabled, the printer settings will be loaded with the document. This can cause a document to be printed on a distant printer, if you do not change the printer manually in the Print dialog. If disabled, your standard printer will be used to print this document. The current printer settings will be stored with the document whether or not this option is checked.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146794				0	lv	Save				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154071				0	lv	Edit document properties before saving				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_DOCINFO\"\>Specifies that the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog will appear every time you select the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> command.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145606				0	lv	Always create backup copy				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_BACKUP\"\>Saves the previous version of a document as a backup copy whenever you save a document. Every time \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> creates a backup copy, the previous backup copy is replaced. The backup copy gets the extension .BAK.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	lv	To change the location of the backup copy, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>, and then enter a new path for the backup file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154908				0	lv	Save AutoRecovery information every				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149560				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_AUTOSAVE\"\>Specifies that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> saves the information needed to restore all open documents in case of a crash. You can specify the saving time interval.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146147				0	lv	Minutes				20200411 15:09:53
