helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010501.xhp	0	help	par_id9701528				0	lv	%PRODUCTNAME uses only the RGB color model for printing in color. The CMYK controls are provided only to ease the input of color values using CMYK notation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010501.xhp	0	help	hd_id5566778801				0	lv	Color Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010501.xhp	0	help	par_id5566778801				0	lv	            \<ahelp hid=\"cui:Control:ColorPicker:ColorField\"\>In the big color field, you click to select a new color.\</ahelp\>        				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010501.xhp	0	help	hd_id5566778802				0	lv	Color Slider				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010501.xhp	0	help	par_id5566778802				0	lv	Click any of the six option buttons Red, Green, Blue, Hue, Saturation, or Brightness. The color slider changes to show the available range of values. \<ahelp hid=\"cui:Control:ColorPicker:ColorSlider\"\>In the color slider, you will see the range of values that you can change, depending on the selected option button. Click inside the color slider to change values in the big color field.\</ahelp\>        				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010501.xhp	0	help	hd_id5566778803				0	lv	Current Color Preview				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010501.xhp	0	help	par_id5566778803				0	lv	            \<ahelp hid=\"cui:Control:ColorPicker:ColorPreview\"\>In the left half of the preview field, you will always see the current result of your work in this dialog.\</ahelp\>        				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010501.xhp	0	help	hd_id5566778803b				0	lv	Previous Color				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010501.xhp	0	help	par_id5566778803b				0	lv	            \<ahelp hid=\"cui:Control:ColorPicker:ColorPrevious\"\>In the right half of the preview field, you will see the original color from the parent tab, \<emph\>Colors\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>        				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010501.xhp	0	help	hd_id5566778804				0	lv	RGB				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010501.xhp	0	help	par_id5566778804				0	lv	These set of controls allow to choose a color in the RGB color model, where red, green, and blue are combined to produce a color.				20200411 15:09:53
