helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN10562				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/guides.xhp\"\>Guides\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the display options for guides.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057B				0	lv	Display Guides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057F				0	lv	Displays or hides guides that you can use to align objects on a page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN10582				0	lv	Snap to Guides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN10586				0	lv	Automatically aligns objects to vertical and horizontal guides. To override this feature, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option key\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt key \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>when you drag an object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C6				0	lv	Guides to Front				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CA				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays the guides in front of the objects on the slide or page.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	HTML import and export				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154380				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>importing; HTML with META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; importing META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; META tags in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tags; META tags\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154380				0	lv	HTML import and export				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	lv	When you export a file to an HTML document, the description and the user-defined file properties are included as META \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tags\"\>tags\</link\> between the HEAD tags of the exported document. META tags are not displayed in a Web browser, and are used to include information, such as keywords for search engines on your Web page. To set the properties of the current document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> or \<emph\>User Defined\</emph\> tabs, and then type the information you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	lv	The following file properties are converted to META tags when you export a file as an HTML document:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3154935				0	lv	File Property				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	lv	<TITLE>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3153778				0	lv	Subject				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	lv	<META NAME="CLASSIFICATION" CONTENT="Field Content">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	lv	Keywords				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	lv	<META NAME="KEYWORDS" CONTENT="Field Content">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	lv	Description				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	lv	<META NAME="DESCRIPTION" CONTENT="Field Content">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	lv	Info fields 1...4				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3157892				0	lv	<META NAME="Info field name" CONTENT="Field Content">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	22			0	lv	When you import an HTML containing these META tags, the contents of the tags are added to the corresponding $[officename] file property box. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id0926200812164481				0	lv	Keywords must be separated by commas. A keyword can contain white space characters or semicolons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163822				0	lv	Import Tips				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155307				0	lv	When you import an HTML document, following META tags are automatically converted to $[officename] fields: <META HTTP-EQUIV="REFRESH"...> and <META NAME="..." ...> , where NAME equals to AUTHOR, CREATED, CHANGED, CHANGEDBY, DESCRIPTION, KEYWORDS or CLASSIFICATION.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3146146				0	lv	Scripts, comments, and META tags that are positioned directly before a TABLE tag are inserted in the first cell of the table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	lv	Scripts and META tags in the header of an HTML document are imported and anchored to the first paragraph in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	lv	To set the options for importing HTML tags, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>. A known META tag contains either "HTTP-EQUIV" or "NAME", and are imported as $[officename] comments. The only exception is <META NAME="GENERATOR"...>, which is ignored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163717				0	lv	Export Tips				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159180				0	lv	Comments and script fields at the beginning of the first paragraph in a document are exported to the header of an HTML document. If the document begins with a table, the first paragraph in the first cell of the table is exported to the header of the HTML document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Asian Typography				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155620				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>Asian typography\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; Asian typography\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; Asian typography\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>typography; Asian\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155620				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020700.xhp\" name=\"Asian Typography\"\>Asian Typography\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	par_id3153124				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Set the typographic options for cells or paragraphs in Asian language files. To enable Asian language support, choose \<emph\>Language Settings - Languages\</emph\> in the Options dialog box, and then select the \<emph\>Enabled\</emph\> box in the \<emph\>Asian language support\</emph\> area.\</ahelp\> The Asian typography options are ignored in HTML documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147571				0	lv	Line change				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834				0	lv	Set the options for line breaks in Asian language documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145072				0	lv	Apply list of forbidden characters to the beginning and end of line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	par_id3153683				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_TRISTATEBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_PARA_ASIAN_CB_AS_FORBIDDEN\"\>Prevents the characters in the list from starting or ending a line. The characters are relocated to either the previous or the next line.\</ahelp\> To edit the list of restricted characters, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01150100.xhp\" name=\"Asian Layout\"\>Asian Layout\</link\>\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149751				0	lv	Allow hanging punctuation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149096				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_TRISTATEBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_PARA_ASIAN_CB_AS_HANG_PUNC\"\>Prevents commas and periods from breaking the line. Instead, these characters are added to the end of the line, even in the page margin.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	lv	\<emph\>Apply spacing between Asian, Latin and Complex text\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_TRISTATEBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_PARA_ASIAN_CB_AS_SCRIPT_SPACE\"\>Inserts a space between Asian, Latin and complex characters.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Enabling Asian language support\"\>Enabling Asian language support\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
