helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts a video or sound file into your document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_idN10683				0	lv	To insert a movie or sound file into your document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	lv	Click where you want to insert the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068E				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Movie and Sound\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_idN10696				0	lv	In the File Open dialog, select the file that you want to insert.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	lv	The file types that are listed in this dialog are not supported by all operating systems.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D7				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_id0120200912190948				0	lv	Alternatively, you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Media Player\</item\> to open the Media Player. Use the Media Player to preview all supported media files. Click the Apply button in the Media Player window to insert the current media file into your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069C				0	lv	To play a movie or sound file				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A7				0	lv	Click the object icon for the movie or sound file in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_id0120200912190940				0	lv	If the icon is arranged on the background, hold down Ctrl while you click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_id0120200912062096				0	lv	The Media Playback toolbar is shown.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_idN10788				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Play\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Media Playback\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_id0120200912062064				0	lv	When you show an Impress presentation, the embedded sound or video on the current slide plays automatically until it's over or until you leave the slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\moviesound.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D0				0	lv	You can also use the Media Playback Bar to pause, to stop, to loop, as well as to adjust the volume or to mute the playback of the file. The current playback position in the file is indicated on the left slider. Use the right slider to adjust the playback volume. For movie files, the bar also contains a list box where you can select the zoom factor for the playback.				20200411 15:09:53
