helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	lv	Images				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	lv	Sets the PDF export options for images inside your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071B				0	lv	EPS images with embedded previews are exported only as previews. EPS images without embedded previews are exported as empty placeholders.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	lv	Lossless compression				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN10719				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Selects a lossless compression of images. All pixels are preserved.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	lv	JPEG compression				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN10734				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Selects a JPEG compression of images. With a high quality level, almost all pixels are preserved. With a low quality level, some pixels get lost and artefacts are introduced, but file sizes are reduced.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	lv	Quality				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the quality level for JPEG compression.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN10767				0	lv	Reduce image resolution				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076B				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Selects to resample or down-size the images to a lower number of pixels per inch.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN10782				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the target resolution for the images.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN10791				0	lv	General				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN10795				0	lv	Sets general PDF export options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id2796411				0	lv	PDF/A-1a				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id5016327				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Converts to the PDF/A-1a format. This is defined as an electronic document file format for long term preservation. All fonts that were used in the source document will be embedded into the generated PDF file. PDF tags will be written.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A0				0	lv	Tagged PDF				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A4				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Selects to write PDF tags. This can increase file size by huge amounts.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B3				0	lv	Tagged PDF contains information about the structure of the document contents. This can help to display the document on devices with different screens, and when using screen reader software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	lv	Export notes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C2				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Selects to export comments of Writer and Calc documents as PDF notes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id8257087				0	lv	Export bookmarks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3479415				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Selects to export bookmarks of Writer documents as PDF bookmarks. Bookmarks are created for all outline paragraphs (Tools - Outline Numbering) and for all table of contents entries for which you did assign hyperlinks in the source document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	lv	Create PDF form				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id4909817				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Choose to create a PDF form. This can be filled out and printed by the user of the PDF document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id6585283				0	lv	Submit format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the format of submitting forms from within the PDF file.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id0901200811454970				0	lv	Select the format of the data that you will receive from the submitter: FDF (Forms Data Format), PDF, HTML, or XML.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_idN10807				0	lv	This setting overrides the control's URL property that you set in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id1026200909535841				0	lv	Allow duplicate field names				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id102620090953596				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Allows to use the same field name for multiple fields in the generated PDF file. If disabled, field names will be exported using generated unique names.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id3946958				0	lv	Export automatically inserted blank pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id8551896				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If switched on, automatically inserted blank pages are being exported to pdf file. This is best if you are printing the pdf file double-sided. Example: In a book a chapter paragraph style is set to always start with an odd numbered page. The previous chapter ends on an odd page. %PRODUCTNAME inserts an even numbered blank page. This option controls whether to export that even numbered page or not.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id3954548				0	lv	Embed standard fonts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id853434896				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Normally the 14 standard Postscript fonts are not embedded in a PDF file, because every PDF reader software already contains these fonts. Enable this option to embed the standard fonts that are installed on your system and that are used in the document.\</ahelp\> Use this option if you expect to have a better looking or more useful standard font than the font that is available in the recipients' PDF reader software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id080420080355360				0	lv	Embed this document inside the PDF				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id0804200803553767				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The document being exported will be embedded inside the PDF file.\</ahelp\> Some PDF tools or %PRODUCTNAME extensions may allow to extract the file from the PDF and save it; in this way, the original %PRODUCTNAME document can be edited back without the need of a PDF editing application.				20200411 15:09:53
