helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149264	29			0	lv	You can copy a table by dragging and dropping the table onto the table area of a database file window. The \<emph\>Copy table \</emph\>dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154926				0	lv	Table name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3144740				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TAB_WIZ_TABLENAME_EDIT\"\>Specifies a name for the copy.\</ahelp\> Some databases only accept names containing eight or fewer characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	lv	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157898				0	lv	Definition and data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150178				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_TAB_WIZ_COPYTABLE_RB_DEFDATA\"\>Creates a 1:1 copy of the database table.\</ahelp\> The table definition and the complete data are copied. The table definition includes the table structure and format from different data fields, including special field properties. The field contents supply the data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	lv	Definition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_TAB_WIZ_COPYTABLE_RB_DEF\"\>Copies only the table definition and not the corresponding data.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	lv	As table view				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153311				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_TAB_WIZ_COPYTABLE_RB_VIEW\"\>If the database supports Views, you can select this option only when a query is copied in a table container. This option enables you to see and edit a query as a normal table view.\</ahelp\> The table will be filtered in the view with a "Select" SQL statement.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155535				0	lv	Append data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_TAB_WIZ_COPYTABLE_RB_APPENDDATA\"\>Appends the data of the table to be copied to an existing table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	lv	The table definition must be exactly the same so that data can be copied. Data cannot be copied if a data field in the target table has another format than the data field in the source table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156117	31			0	lv	Match the data field names in the\<emph\> Copy Table\</emph\> dialog on the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05030400.xhp\" name=\"Apply Columns\"\>Apply Columns\</link\> page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_TAB_WIZ_COPYTABLE_RB_APPENDDATA\"\>If the data cannot be attached, you will see a list of fields in the \<emph\>Column Info\</emph\> dialog whose data cannot be copied.\</ahelp\> If you confirm this dialog with OK, only the data that does not appear in the list will be attached.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	lv	If the fields of the target table have a smaller field length than in the source table when data is being attached, the source data fields will automatically be truncated to match the field lengths in the target table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149164				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>primary keys; defining\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
