helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	ODBC				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149031				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/11020000.xhp\" name=\"ODBC\"\>ODBC\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"\"\>Specifies the settings for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#odbc\" name=\"ODBC\"\>ODBC\</link\> databases. This includes your user access data, driver settings, and font definitions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148642				0	lv	User Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Type the user name for accessing the database.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153665				0	lv	Password required				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Prevents an unauthorized user from accessing the database. You only need to enter the password once per session.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087				0	lv	Driver Settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_ODBC_OPTIONS\"\>Use this text field to enter additional optional driver settings if this is necessary.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152472				0	lv	Character Set				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_CHARSET_ODBC\"\>Select the code conversion that you want to use to view the database in $[officename]. This does not affect the database.\</ahelp\> Choose "System" to use the default character set of your operating system. Text and dBASE databases are restricted to character sets with a fixed-size character length, where all characters are encoded with the same number of bytes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149669				0	lv	General				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147265				0	lv	Retrieve generated values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_AUTORETRIEVEENABLED\"\>Enables $[officename] support of auto-incremented data fields for the current ODBC or JDBC data source.\</ahelp\> Select this check box if the database does not support the auto-increment feature in its SDBCX layer. In general, the auto-increment is selected for the primary key field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400				0	lv	Auto-increment statement				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366	27			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_AUTOINCREMENTVALUE\"\>Enter the SQL command specifier that instructs the data source to auto-increment a specified Integer data field.\</ahelp\> For example, a typical SQL statement to create a data field is: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	lv	CREATE TABLE "table1" ("id" INTEGER)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	lv	To auto-increment the "id" data field in a MySQL database, change the statement to:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909				0	lv	CREATE TABLE "table1" ("id" INTEGER AUTO_INCREMENT)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	lv	In other words, enter AUTO_INCREMENT into \<emph\>Auto-increment statement\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149765				0	lv	Query of generated values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_RETRIEVE_AUTO\"\>Enter an SQL statement that returns the last auto-incremented value for the primary key data field.\</ahelp\> For example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150769				0	lv	SELECT LAST_INSERT_D();				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157892				0	lv	Use SQL92 naming constraints				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_SQL92CHECK\"\>Only allows names that use characters that conform to the SQL92 naming constraints in the data source. All other characters are rejected.\</ahelp\> Each name must begin with a lower or upper case letter, or an underline ( _ ). The remaining characters can be ASCII letters, underlines, and numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154011				0	lv	Use Catalog for file-based databases				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_USECATALOG\"\>Uses the current data source of the Catalog. This is useful when the ODBC data source is a database server. If the ODBC data source is a dBASE driver, leave this check box clear.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Queries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150445				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>queries;overview (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; printing queries (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; queries (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries; printing (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02000000.xhp\" name=\"Queries\"\>Queries\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499				0	lv	A "query" is a special view of a table. A query can display chosen records or chosen fields within records; it can also sort those records. A query can apply to one table to multiple tables, if they are linked by common data fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	lv	Use queries to find records from data tables based on certain criteria. All queries created for a database are listed under the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> entry. Since this entry contains the database queries, it is also called the "query container".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153750				0	lv	Printing Queries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149183				0	lv	To print a query or table:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	lv	Open a text document (or a spreadsheet document if you prefer the specific printing functions of this type of document).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	lv	Open the database file and click the Table icon if you want to print a table, or click the Query icon if you want to print a query.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	lv	Drag the name of the table or query into the open text document or spreadsheet. The dialog \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Database Columns\"\>Insert Database Columns\</link\> opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	lv	Decide which columns = data fields you want to include. You can also click the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> button and select a corresponding formatting type. Close the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	lv	The query or table will be inserted into your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	lv	Print the document by choosing \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153146				0	lv	You can also open the data source view (F4), select the entire database table in the data source view (button in the top left corner of the table), and then drag the selection to a text document or spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0212.xhp\" name=\"Sorting and Filtering Data\"\>Sorting and Filtering Data\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	lv	Allows you to sort and filter the data in a query table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	lv	With the \<emph\>Query Design\</emph\>, you can create and edit a query or view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Through Several Tables\"\>Query Through Several Tables\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151043				0	lv	The query result can contain data from several tables if these are linked to each other by suitable data fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159149				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Formulating Query Criteria\"\>Formulating Query Criteria\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910				0	lv	You can find out which operators and commands can be used to formulate the filter conditions for a query.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156212				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Executing Functions\"\>Executing Functions\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	lv	You can perform calculations with the data of a table and store the results as a query result.				20200411 15:09:53
