helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id7679372				0	lv	In a database window, choose \<emph\>Edit - Database - Advanced Settings\</emph\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id4572283				0	lv	The availability of the following controls depends on the type of database:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10590				0	lv	Use SQL92 naming constraints				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10594				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Only allows characters that conform to the SQL92 naming convention in a name in a data source. All other characters are rejected. Each name must begin with a lowercase letter, an uppercase letter, or an underscore ( _ ). The remaining characters can be ASCII letters, numbers, and underscores.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105907				0	lv	Use keyword AS before table alias names				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105947				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Some databases use the keyword "AS" between a name and its alias, while other databases use a whitespace. Enable this option to insert AS before the alias.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3534958				0	lv	End text lines with CR + LF				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id6151921				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select to use the CR + LF code pair to end every text line (preferred for DOS and Windows operating systems).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059E				0	lv	Append the table alias name in SELECT statements				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A2				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Appends the alias to the table name in SELECT statements.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A5				0	lv	Use Outer Join syntax '{OJ }'				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A9				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use escape sequences for outer joins. The syntax for this escape sequence is {oj outer-join}\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105BE				0	lv	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	lv	select Article.* from {oj item LEFT OUTER JOIN orders ON item.no=orders.ANR}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	lv	Ignore the privileges from the database driver				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Ignores access privileges that are provided by the database driver.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CB				0	lv	Replace named parameters with ?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Replaces named parameters in a data source with a question mark (?).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D2				0	lv	Display version columns (when available)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D6				0	lv	Some databases assign version numbers to fields to track changes to records. The version number of a field is incremented by one each time the contents of the field are changed. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_SUPPRESS_VERSIONCL\"\>Displays the internal version number of the record in the database table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FA				0	lv	Use the catalog name in SELECT statements				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FE				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Uses the current data source of the catalog. This option is useful when the ODBC data source is a database server. Do not select this option if the ODBC data source is a dBASE driver.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10613				0	lv	Use the schema name in SELECT statements				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Allows you to use the schema name in SELECT statements.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	lv	Create index with ASC or DESC statement				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Creates an index with ASC or DESC statements.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
