helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091500.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155961				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] Math;reference list\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas;reference tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reference tables; formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>operators;in Math\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	lv	\<variable id=\"reference\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091500.xhp\" name=\"Formula Reference Tables\"\>Formula Reference Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149502				0	lv	\<variable id=\"ref\"\>This reference section contains lists of many operators, functions, symbols and formatting features available in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>. Many of the commands displayed can be inserted using the icons in the \<emph\>Elements\</emph\> window or the context menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090900.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	$[officename] Math Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090900.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151265				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>examples;$[officename] Math formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] Math;examples\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas;examples\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151265				0	lv	\<variable id=\"examples\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090900.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Math Examples\"\>$[officename] Math Examples\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090900.xhp	0	help	par_id3153624				0	lv	The following is a list of sample formulas in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Display All				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03060000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147340				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>views; maximum size\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>maximum formula size\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; maximum size\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03060000.xhp\" name=\"Show All\"\>Show All / Display All\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148571				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays the entire formula in the maximum size possible so that all elements are included. The formula is reduced or enlarged so that all formula elements can be displayed in the work area.\</ahelp\> The current zoom factor is displayed on the status bar. A selection of available zoom options is accessible through the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\>. The context menu in the work area also contains zoom commands. The name of the icon is "Show All", the name of the context menu command is "Display All". The zoom commands and icons are only available in Math documents, not for embedded Math objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090901.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Symbols with Indices				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090901.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090901.xhp\" name=\"Symbols with Indices\"\>Symbols with Indices\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090901.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301				0	lv	The following example explains how to create symbols with indexes in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>. You can copy this example to the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window by using the clipboard and use it in your own formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090901.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3148870\" src=\"res/helpimg/smzb1.png\" width=\"3.217cm\" height=\"2.939cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148870\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Set Operations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156318				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>set operations in $[officename]Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sets of numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>included in set operator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>not included in set operator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>owns command\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>includes set operator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>empty set\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>intersection of sets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>union of sets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>difference set operator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>quotient set\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cardinal numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subset set operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>superset set operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>not subset set operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>not superset set operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>natural numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>whole numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>real numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>complex numbers; set\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rational numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156318				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090800.xhp\" name=\"Set Operations\"\>Set Operations\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154641	2			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_SETOPERATIONS_CAT\"\>Assign different set operators to the characters in your \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\> formula. The individual operators are shown in the lower section of the Elements window\</ahelp\>. Call the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to see an identical list of the individual functions. Any operators not found in the Elements window have to be entered directly in the Commands window. You can also directly insert other parts of the formula even if symbols already exist for them.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3149290				0	lv	After clicking the \<emph\>Set Operations\</emph\> icon in the Elements window additional icons will be shown in the lower part of this window. Simply click a symbol to incorporate the operator in the formula being edited in the Commands window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147258				0	lv	The set operations in detail:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_idN10081				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3145418\" src=\"starmath/res/op21401.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145418\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154275				0	lv	is included in				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3150706				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XINY\"\>Use the icon to insert the \<emph\>is included in\</emph\> set operator with two placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also enter \<emph\><?> in <?>\</emph\> directly into the Commands window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_idN100BC				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3153782\" src=\"starmath/res/op21402.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153782\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
