helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id6006958				0	lv	On the first page of the Chart Wizard you can \<link href=\"text/schart/01/choose_chart_type.xhp\"\>choose a chart type\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	hd_id3919186				0	lv	To choose a chart type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3453169				0	lv	Choose a basic \<link href=\"text/schart/01/choose_chart_type.xhp\"\>chart type\</link\>: click any of the entries labeled Column, Bar, Pie, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id8406933				0	lv	The contents on the right side will change to offer more options depending on the basic chart type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id8230231				0	lv	Optionally, click any of the options. While you change the settings in the wizard, watch the preview in the document to see how the chart will look.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3267006				0	lv	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F1\</item\> and point to a control to see an extended help text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7251503				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\> on any wizard page to close the wizard and create the chart using the current settings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3191625				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> to see the next wizard page, or click the entries on the left side of the wizard to go to that page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7659535				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Back\</emph\> to see the previous wizard page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id8420056				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> to close the wizard without creating a chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id2284920				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to go to the named wizard page.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3184301				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a basic chart type.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id2129276				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a sub type of the basic chart type.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id9719229				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enables a 3D look for the data values.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3860896				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the type of 3D look.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id4041871				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a shape from the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id9930722				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays stacked series for Line charts.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id5749687				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Stack series display values on top of each other.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id79348				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Stack series display values as percent.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id2414014				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The lines are shown as curves.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7617114				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog to set the curve properties.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id6649372				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Connects points by ascending X values, even if the order of values is different, in an XY scatter diagram.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7334208				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Set the number of lines for the Column and Line chart type.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id4485000				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Chart Type dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Data Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150869				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/03010000.xhp\" name=\"Data Table\"\>Data Table\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115	2			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramData\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Data Table \</emph\>dialog where you can edit the chart data.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667	51			0	lv	The\<emph\> Data Table \</emph\>dialog is not available if you insert a chart that is based on a Calc sheet or on a Writer table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id6746421				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06990000.xhp\"\>To update a chart manually when a Writer table got changed\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id2565996				0	lv	Some changes will become visible only after you close and reopen the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id6129947				0	lv	To change chart data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id8141117				0	lv	When you create a chart that is based on default data, or when you copy a chart into your document, you can open the Data Table dialog to enter your own data. The chart responds to the data in a live preview.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id9487594				0	lv	Close the Chart Data dialog to apply all changes to the chart. Choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\> to cancel the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id4149906				0	lv	Insert or select a chart that is not based on existing cell data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id6064943				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>View - Chart Data Table\</emph\> to open the Data Table dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	lv	The data series are organized in columns. The role of the left most column is set to categories or data labels respectively. The contents of the left most column are always formatted as text. You can insert more text columns to be used as hierarchical labels.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id9799798				0	lv	Click a cell in the dialog and change the contents. Click another cell to see the changed contents in the preview.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	lv	Enter the name of the data series in the text box above the column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id743430				0	lv	Use the icons above the table to insert or delete rows and columns. For data series with multiple columns, only whole data series can be inserted or deleted. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	lv	The order of the data series in the chart is the same as in the data table. Use the \<emph\>Move Series Right\</emph\> icon to switch the current column with its neighbor on the right.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id9116794				0	lv	The order of the categories or data points in the chart is the same as in the data table. Use the \<emph\>Move Row Down\</emph\> icon to switch the current row with its neighbor below.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150297				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new row below the current row.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new data series after the current column.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152297				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new text column after the current column for hierarchical axes descriptions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159231				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the current row. It is not possible to delete the label row.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153336				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the current series or text column. It is not possible to delete the first text column.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id4089175				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Switches the current column with its neighbor at the right.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3949095				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Switches the current row with its neighbor below.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id6697286				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter names for the data series.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Data Series				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150449				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010200.xhp\" name=\"Data Series\"\>Data Series\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	lv	Use this to change the properties of a selected data series. This dialog appears when one data series is selected when you choose \<emph\>Format - Format Selection\</emph\>. Some of the menu entries are only available for 2D or 3D charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015				0	lv	Any changes made here affect the entire data series. For example, if you change the color, all elements belonging to this data series will change color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146916				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Y Error Bars\"\>Y Error Bars\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Alignment				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149656				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05020201.xhp\" name=\"Alignment\"\>Alignment\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	lv	Modifies the alignment of axes or title labels.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	lv	Some of the options listed here are not available for all labels. For example, there are different options for 2D and 3D object labels.				20200411 15:09:53
