helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149334				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CirclePie_Unfilled\"\>Draws an empty shape that is defined by the arc of a circle and two radius lines in the current document. To draw a circle pie, drag a circle to the size you want, and then click to define the first radius line. Move your pointer to where you want to place the second radius line and click. You do not need to click on the circle. To draw an ellipse pie, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154199				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3146925\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlepie_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3146925\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148986				0	lv	Circle Pie, Unfilled				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149300				0	lv	Ellipse Segment, Unfilled				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155179				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:EllipseCut_Unfilled\"\>Draws an empty shape that is defined by the arc of an oval and a diameter line in the current document. To draw an ellipse segment, drag an ellipse to the size you want, and then click to define the starting point of the diameter line. Move your pointer to where you want to place the endpoint of the diameter line and click. You do not need to click on the ellipse. To draw a circle segment, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149483				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3149490\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_ellipsecut_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149490\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
