helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Creating a Custom Slide Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>slide shows; custom\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting; always with the current slide\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting;custom slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;hidden slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden pages;showing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	lv	\<variable id=\"individual\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/individual.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Custom Slide Show\"\>Creating a Custom Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150344				0	lv	You can create custom slide shows to meet the needs of your audience using slides within the current presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	lv	To create a custom slide show:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153712				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Shows\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966	62			0	lv	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and enter a name for your slide show in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249				0	lv	Under \<emph\>Existing Slides\</emph\>, select the slides you want to add to your slide show, and click the \<emph\>>>\</emph\> button. Hold down Shift to select a range of slides, or Ctrl to select multiple slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153916				0	lv	You can change the order of the slides in your custom slide show, by dragging and dropping the slides under \<emph\>Selected Slides\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151387				0	lv	To start a custom slide show:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3147403				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	lv	Select the show you want to start from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3149943				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Start\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3145593	56			0	lv	If you want the selected custom slide show to start when you click the \<emph\>Slide Show\</emph\> icon on the\<emph\> Presentation\</emph\> toolbar, or when you press F5, select \<emph\>Use Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145169				0	lv	Options for Running a Slide Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150335				0	lv	To always start a slide show from the current slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150014				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155932				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Start presentation\</emph\> area, select the \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155372				0	lv	Do not select this option if you want to run a custom slide show.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153922				0	lv	To hide a slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id883150344				0	lv	To hide the current slide, click the Hide Slide action button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	lv	To hide several slides, choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>, and then select the slide(s) that you want to hide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3083278				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3151264				0	lv	The slide is not removed from your document.				20200411 15:09:53
