helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150021				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145244				0	lv	To use an image for the slide background				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148394				0	lv	You can display an entire image as a slide background, or you can tile the image to produce a patterned background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156064				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3145356	59			0	lv	In the \<emph\>Fill \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>, and then click an image in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150757	60			0	lv	If you want to use a custom image for the slide background, close the \<emph\>Page Setup \</emph\>dialog, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Bitmaps \</emph\>tab, and then click \<emph\>Import\</emph\>. Locate the image you want to import and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When you return to the \<emph\>Background \</emph\>tab, the image you imported will be in the \<emph\>Bitmap \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153151				0	lv	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150263	62			0	lv	To display the entire image as the background, clear the \<emph\>Tile \</emph\>check box in the \<emph\>Position \</emph\>area, and then select \<emph\>AutoFit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149756				0	lv	To tile the image on the background, select \<emph\>Tile\</emph\>, and set the \<emph\>Size\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> options for the image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154934				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3158403				0	lv	This modification is only valid for the current presentation document.				20200411 15:09:53
