helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	lv	Refer also to the lists of shortcut keys for \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> in general.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	lv	Cell Selection Mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3150439\" src=\"formula/res/refinp1.png\" width=\"0.1327inch\" height=\"0.1327inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150439\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	lv	In a text box that has a button to minimize the dialog, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> to enter the cell selection mode. Select any number of cells, then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> again to show the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	lv	In the cell selection mode, you can use the common navigation keys to select cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148646				0	lv	Controlling the Outline				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	lv	You can use the keyboard in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Outline\"\>Outline\</link\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	lv	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F6\</item\> until the vertical or horizontal outline window has the focus.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	lv	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons from top to bottom or from left to right.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	lv	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons in the opposite direction.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149403				0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+1 to Command+8\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+8\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - show all levels up to the specified number; hide all higher levels.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	lv	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>+\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>-\</item\> to show or hide the focused outline group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	lv	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to activate the focused button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	lv	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\>, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow to cycle through all buttons in the current level.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147343				0	lv	Selecting a Drawing Object or a Graphic				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AA				0	lv	Choose View - Toolbars - Drawing to open the Drawing toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	lv	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> until the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	lv	If the selection tool is active, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. This selects the first drawing object or graphic in the sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159240				0	lv	With \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 you set the focus to the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379				0	lv	Now you can use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to select the next drawing object or graphic and \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to select the previous one.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Printing Sheets in Landscape Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing in landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing; landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape printing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	lv	\<variable id=\"print_landscape\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_landscape.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\"\>Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257				0	lv	In order to print a sheet you have a number of interactive options available under \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>. Drag the delimiter lines to define the range of printed cells on each page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	lv	To print in landscape format, proceed as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	lv	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089	5			0	lv	The command is not visible if the sheet has been opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430				0	lv	Select the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab. Select the \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\> paper format and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150885				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288				0	lv	Depending on the printer driver and the operating system, it may be necessary to click the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button and to change your printer to landscape format there.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404	9			0	lv	In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>dialog in the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page, select the contents to be printed:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	10			0	lv	               \<emph\>All sheets\</emph\> - All sheets will be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148871	12			0	lv	               \<emph\>Selected sheets\</emph\> - Only the selected sheets will be printed. All sheets whose names (at the bottom on the sheet tabs) are selected will be printed. By pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while clicking a sheet name you can change this selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3764763				0	lv	               \<emph\>Selected cells\</emph\> - All selected cells are printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id5538804				0	lv	From all the paper pages that result from the above selection, you can select the range of paper pages to be printed:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id14343				0	lv	               \<emph\>All pages\</emph\> - Print all resulting pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699	11			0	lv	               \<emph\>Pages\</emph\> - Enter the pages to be printed. The pages will also be numbered from the first sheet onwards. If you see in the Page Break Preview that Sheet1 will be printed on 4 pages and you want to print the first two pages of Sheet2, enter 5-6 here.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3145076				0	lv	If under \<emph\>Format - Print ranges\</emph\> you have defined one or more print ranges, only the contents of these print ranges will be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id8254646				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp\"\>Defining Print Ranges on a Sheet\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Applying Conditional Formatting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149263				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>conditional formatting; cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; conditional formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; conditional formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;conditional styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell formats; conditional\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>random numbers;examples\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell styles; copying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; cell styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; copying cell styles\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149263				0	lv	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_conditional\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_conditional.xhp\" name=\"Applying Conditional Formatting\"\>Applying Conditional Formatting\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156				0	lv	Using the menu command \<emph\>Format - Conditional formatting\</emph\>, the dialog allows you to define up to three conditions per cell, which must be met in order for the selected cells to have a particular format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id8039796				0	lv	To apply conditional formatting, AutoCalculate must be enabled. Choose \<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoCalculate\</emph\> (you see a check mark next to the command when AutoCalculate is enabled).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	lv	With conditional formatting, you can, for example, highlight the totals that exceed the average value of all totals. If the totals change, the formatting changes correspondingly, without having to apply other styles manually.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id4480727				0	lv	To Define the Conditions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	lv	Select the cells to which you want to apply a conditional style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Conditional Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	lv	Enter the condition(s) into the dialog box. The dialog is described in detail in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>, and an example is provided below:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	lv	Example of Conditional Formatting: Highlighting Totals Above/Under the Average Value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id4341868				0	lv	Step1: Generate Number Values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	lv	You want to give certain values in your tables particular emphasis. For example, in a table of turnovers, you can show all the values above the average in green and all those below the average in red. This is possible with conditional formatting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	lv	First of all, write a table in which a few different values occur. For your test you can create tables with any random numbers:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	lv	In one of the cells enter the formula =RAND(), and you will obtain a random number between 0 and 1. If you want integers of between 0 and 50, enter the formula =INT(RAND()*50).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	lv	Copy the formula to create a row of random numbers. Click the bottom right corner of the selected cell, and drag to the right until the desired cell range is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	lv	In the same way as described above, drag down the corner of the rightmost cell in order to create more rows of random numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149211				0	lv	Step 2: Define Cell Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	lv	The next step is to apply a cell style to all values that represent above-average turnover, and one to those that are below the average. Ensure that the Styles and Formatting window is visible before proceeding.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	lv	Click in a blank cell and select the command \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> in the context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab, select a background color. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	lv	In the Styles and Formatting window, click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon. Enter the name of the new style. For this example, name the style "Above".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889				0	lv	To define a second style, click again in a blank cell and proceed as described above. Assign a different background color for the cell and assign a name (for this example, "Below").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148704				0	lv	Step 3: Calculate Average				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837				0	lv	In our particular example, we are calculating the average of the random values. The result is placed in a cell:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	lv	Set the cursor in a blank cell, for example, J14, and choose \<emph\>Insert - Function\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3156016				0	lv	Select the AVERAGE function. Use the mouse to select all your random numbers. If you cannot see the entire range, because the Function Wizard is obscuring it, you can temporarily shrink the dialog using the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#eingabesymbol\" name=\"Shrink or Maximize\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Shrink / Maximize\</item\>\</link\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246				0	lv	Close the Function Wizard with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149898				0	lv	Step 4: Apply Cell Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	lv	Now you can apply the conditional formatting to the sheet:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150049				0	lv	Select all cells with the random numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153801				0	lv	Choose the \<emph\>Format - Conditional Formatting\</emph\> command to open the corresponding dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153013				0	lv	Define the condition as follows: If cell value is less than J14, format with cell style "Below", and if cell value is greater than or equal to J14, format with cell style "Above".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155761				0	lv	Step 5: Copy Cell Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3145320				0	lv	To apply the conditional formatting to other cells later:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153074				0	lv	Click one of the cells that has been assigned conditional formatting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149051				0	lv	Copy the cell to the clipboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150436				0	lv	Select the cells that are to receive this same formatting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3147298				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> area, check only the \<emph\>Formats\</emph\> box. All other boxes must be unchecked. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159123				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Conditional formatting\"\>Format - Conditional formatting\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150542				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150542				0	lv	\<variable id=\"html_doc\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/html_doc.xhp\" name=\"Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\"\>Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154124				0	lv	Saving Sheets in HTML				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	lv	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc saves all the sheets of a Calc document together as an HTML document. At the beginning of the HTML document, a heading and a list of hyperlinks are automatically added which lead to the individual sheets within the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	lv	Numbers are shown as written. In addition, in the <SDVAL> HTML tag, the exact internal number value is written so that after opening the HTML document with \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you know you have the exact values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	lv	To save the current Calc document as HTML, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	lv	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> list box, in the area with the other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc filters, choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	lv	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149379				0	lv	Opening Sheets in HTML				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	lv	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> offers various filters for opening HTML files, which you can select under \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Files of type\</emph\> list box:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	lv	Choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	lv	All \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc options are now available to you. However, not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc offers for editing can be saved in HTML format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"File - Save As\"\>File - Save As\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Pivot Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150448				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; introduction\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot, see pivot table function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150448				0	lv	\<variable id=\"datapilot\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot.xhp\" name=\"Pivot Table\"\>Pivot Table\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	lv	The \<emph\>pivot table\</emph\> (formerly known as \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\>) allows you to combine, compare, and analyze large amounts of data. You can view different summaries of the source data, you can display the details of areas of interest, and you can create reports.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	lv	A table that has been created as a \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090000.xhp\" name=\"pivot table\"\>pivot table\</link\> is an interactive table. Data can be arranged, rearranged or summarized according to different points of view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Navigating Through Sheets Tabs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; showing multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769	4			0	lv	\<variable id=\"multi_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multi_tables.xhp\" name=\"Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\"\>Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	lv	By default $[officename] displays three sheets "Sheet1" to "Sheet3", in each new spreadsheet. You can switch between sheets in a spreadsheet using the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	lv	 \<image id=\"img_id4829822\" src=\"res/helpimg/sheettabs.png\" width=\"3.3335inch\" height=\"0.7638inch\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4829822\"\>Sheet Tabs\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	lv	 \<image id=\"img_id3156441\" src=\"res/helpimg/calcnav.png\" width=\"0.6563inch\" height=\"0.1457inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156441\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	lv	Use the navigation buttons to display all the sheets belonging to your document. Clicking the button on the far left or the far right displays, respectively, the first or last sheet tab. The middle buttons allow the user to scroll forward and backward through all sheet tabs. To display the sheet itself click on the sheet tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	lv	If there is insufficient space to display all the sheet tabs, you can increase it by pointing to the separator between the scrollbar and the sheet tabs, pressing the mouse button and, keeping the mouse button pressed, dragging to the right. In doing so you will be sharing the available space between the sheet tabs and horizontal scrollbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Unprotecting Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153252				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>cell protection; unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protecting; unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153252	14			0	lv	\<variable id=\"cell_unprotect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_unprotect.xhp\" name=\"Unprotecting Cells\"\>Unprotecting Cells\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	lv	Click the sheet for which you want to cancel the protection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	lv	Select \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, then choose \<emph\>Sheet\</emph\> or \<emph\>Document\</emph\> to remove the check mark indicating the protected status.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	lv	If you have assigned a password, enter it in this dialog and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	lv	The cells can now be edited, the formulas can be viewed, and all cells can be printed until you reactivate the protection for the sheet or document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Applying AutoFilter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>filters, see also AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoFilter function;applying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; filter values\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; filter sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drop-down menus in sheet columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>database ranges; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	lv	\<variable id=\"autofilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autofilter.xhp\" name=\"Applying AutoFilter\"\>Applying AutoFilter\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	lv	The \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function inserts a combo box on one or more data columns that lets you select the records (rows) to be displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	lv	Select the columns you want to use AutoFilter on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>. The combo box arrows are visible in the first row of the range selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	lv	Run the filter by clicking the drop-down arrow in the column heading and choosing an item.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	lv	Only those rows whose contents meet the filter criteria are displayed. The other rows are filtered. You can see if rows have been filtered from the discontinuous row numbers. The column that has been used for the filter is identified by a different color for the arrow button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id9216589				0	lv	When you apply an additional AutoFilter on another column of a filtered data range, then the other combo boxes list only the filtered data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	12			0	lv	To display all records again, select the "all\<emph\>"\</emph\> entry in the AutoFilter combo box. If you choose "Standard\<emph\>"\</emph\>, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Standard Filter\</item\> dialog appears, allowing you to set up a standard filter. Choose "Top 10" to display the highest 10 values only. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	lv	To stop using AutoFilter, reselect all cells selected in step 1 and once again choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id4303415				0	lv	To assign different AutoFilters to different sheets, you must first define a database range on each sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	lv	The arithmetic functions also take account of the cells that are not visible due to an applied filter. For example, a sum of an entire column will also total the values in the filtered cells. Apply the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\> function if only the cells visible after the application of a filter are to be taken into account.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040100.xhp\" name=\"Data - Filter - AutoFilter\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Calculating With Formulas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>formulas;calculating with\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; with formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;formula calculation\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	lv	\<variable id=\"formulas\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formulas.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Formulas\"\>Calculating With Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	lv	All formulas begin with an equals sign. The formulas can contain numbers, text, arithmetic operators, logic operators, or functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	lv	Remember that the basic arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /) can be used in formulas using the "Multiplication and Division before Addition and Subtraction" rule. Instead of writing =SUM(A1:B1) you can write =A1+B1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	lv	Parentheses can also be used. The result of the formula =(1+2)*3 produces a different result than =1+2*3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156285				0	lv	Here are a few examples of $[officename] Calc formulas:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015				0	lv	=A1+10				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	lv	Displays the contents of cell A1 plus 10.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	lv	=A1*16%				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	lv	Displays 16% of the contents of A1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146917				0	lv	=A1 * A2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146315				0	lv	Displays the result of the multiplication of A1 and A2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	lv	=ROUND(A1;1)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363				0	lv	Displays the contents of cell A1 rounded to one decimal place.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150209				0	lv	=EFFECTIVE(5%;12)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	lv	Calculates the effective interest for 5% annual nominal interest with 12 payments a year.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114				0	lv	=B8-SUM(B10:B14)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	lv	Calculates B8 minus the sum of the cells B10 to B14.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152890				0	lv	=SUM(B8;SUM(B10:B14))				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	lv	Calculates the sum of cells B10 to B14 and adds the value to B8.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109				0	lv	It is also possible to nest functions in formulas, as shown in the example. You can also nest functions within functions. The Function Wizard assists you with nested functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060100.xhp\" name=\"Functions list\"\>Functions list\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"AutoPilot: Functions\"\>Function Wizard\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Only Copy Visible Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150440				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>cells; copying/deleting/formatting/moving\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows;visible and invisible\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>moving;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>invisible cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>filters;copying visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hidden cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	lv	\<variable id=\"cellcopy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellcopy.xhp\" name=\"Only Copy Visible Cells\"\>Only Copy Visible Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3148577				0	lv	Assume you have hidden a few rows in a cell range. Now you want to copy, delete, or format only the remaining visible rows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	lv	$[officename] behavior depends on how the cells were made invisible, by a filter or manually.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	lv	Method and Action				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150751				0	lv	Result				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	lv	Cells were filtered by AutoFilters, standard filters or advanced filters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044				0	lv	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	lv	Only the visible cells of the selection are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3166427				0	lv	Cells were hidden using the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> command in the context menu of the row or column headers, or through an \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"outline\"\>outline\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	lv	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	lv	All cells of the selection, including the hidden cells, are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Selecting Themes for Sheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>theme selection for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layout;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	6			0	lv	\<variable id=\"design\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/design.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Themes for Sheets\"\>Selecting Themes for Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	lv	$[officename] Calc comes with a predefined set of formatting themes that you can apply to your spreadsheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	lv	It is not possible to add themes to Calc, and they cannot be modified. However, you can modify their styles after you apply them to a spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	lv	Before you format a sheet with a theme, you have to apply at least one custom cell style to the cells on the sheet. You can then change the cell formatting by selecting and applying a theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	lv	To apply a custom cell style to a cell, you can open the Styles and Formatting window and, in its lower list box, set the Custom Styles view. A list of the existing custom defined cell styles will be displayed. Double click a name from the Styles and Formatting window to apply this style to the selected cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	lv	To apply a theme to a spreadsheet:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	15			0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Choose Themes\</emph\> icon in the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> bar. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	lv	The \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog appears. This dialog lists the available themes for the whole spreadsheet and the Styles and Formatting window lists the custom styles for specific cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	9			0	lv	In the \<emph\>Theme Selection \</emph\>dialog, select the theme that you want to apply to the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	lv	Click OK				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150201				0	lv	As soon as you select another theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog, some of the properties of the custom style will be applied to the current spreadsheet. The modifications will be immediately visible in your spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146979				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/scalc/02/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Theme selection\"\>Theme selection\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155686				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; moving cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; moving by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;moving by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;cells by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cells, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id986358				0	lv	\<variable id=\"move_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/move_dragdrop.xhp\"\>Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2760093				0	lv	When you drag-and-drop a selection of cells on a Calc sheet, the cells normally overwrite the existing cells in the area where you drop. This is the normal \<emph\>overwrite mode\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9527268				0	lv	When you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while releasing the mouse button, you enter the \<emph\>insert mode\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id79653				0	lv	In insert mode, the existing cells where you drop will be shifted to the right or to the bottom, and the dropped cells are inserted into the now empty positions without overwriting. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8676717				0	lv	The surrounding box of the moved cells looks different in insert mode. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3968932				0	lv	In overwrite mode you see all four borders around the selected area. In insert mode you see only the left border when target cells will be shifted to the right. You see only the upper border when target cells will be shifted down. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id7399517				0	lv	Whether the target area will be shifted to the right or to the bottom depends on the distance between source and target cells, if you move within the same sheet. It depends on the number of horizontal or vertical cells in the moved area, if you move to a different sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8040406				0	lv	If you move cells in insert mode within the same row (only horizontally), then after insertion of the cells, all cells will be shifted to the left to fill the source area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2586748				0	lv	In both modes, you can hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key, or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys while you release the mouse button to insert a copy or a link, respectively.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5814081				0	lv	Keys pressed while releasing the mouse button				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6581316				0	lv	Result				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9906613				0	lv	No key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2815637				0	lv	Cells are moved and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells are emptied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6161687				0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4278389				0	lv	Cells are copied and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2805566				0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5369121				0	lv	Links to the source cells are inserted and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9518723				0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	lv	Cells are moved and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells are emptied, except if you move within the same rows on the same sheet. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4021423				0	lv	If you move within the same rows on the same sheet, the cells in the target area shift to the right, and then the whole row shifts to fill the source area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2783898				0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2785119				0	lv	Cells are copied and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id584124				0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5590990				0	lv	Links to the source cells are inserted and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Entering a Number with Leading Zeros				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147560				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>zero values; entering leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>integers with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; changing text/number\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; changing to numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text with leading zeros, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147560				0	lv	\<variable id=\"integer_leading_zero\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/integer_leading_zero.xhp\" name=\"Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\"\>Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	lv	There are various ways to enter integers starting with a zero:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	lv	Enter the number as text. The easiest way is to enter the number starting with an apostrophe (for example, \<item type=\"input\"\>'0987\</item\>). The apostrophe will not appear in the cell, and the number will be formatted as text. Because it is in text format, however, you cannot calculate with this number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	lv	Format a cell with a number format such as \<item type=\"input\"\>\\0000\</item\>. This format can be assigned in the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> field under the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab, and defines the cell display as "always put a zero first and then the integer, having at least three places, and filled with zeros at the left if less than three digits".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	lv	If you want to apply a numerical format to a column of numbers in text format (for example, text "000123" becomes number "123"), do the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	lv	Select the column in which the digits are found in text format. Set the cell format in that column as "Number".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	60			0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	61			0	lv	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>^[0-9]\</item\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	62			0	lv	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>&\</item\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	63			0	lv	Check \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	64			0	lv	Check \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	65			0	lv	Click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	User-defined Number Formats				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143268				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;user-defined formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; user-defined numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; millions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>format codes; user-defined number formats\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143268				0	lv	\<variable id=\"format_value_userdef\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value_userdef.xhp\" name=\"User-defined Number Formats\"\>User-defined Number Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	lv	You can define your own number formats to display numbers in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	lv	As an example, to display the number 10,200,000 as 10.2 Million:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	lv	Select the cells to which you want to apply a new, user-defined format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Categories\</emph\> list box select "User-defined".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> text box enter the following code:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	lv	0.0,, "Million"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	lv	Click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	lv	The following table shows the effects of rounding, thousands delimiters (,), decimal delimiters (.) and the placeholders # and 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	lv	Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	lv	.#,, "Million"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	lv	0.0,, "Million"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920				0	lv	#,, "Million"				20200411 15:09:53
