helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166122				0	lv	TREND(DataY; DataX; NewDataX; LinearType)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166137				0	lv	\<emph\>DataY\</emph\> represents the Y Data array.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166156				0	lv	\<emph\>DataX\</emph\> (optional) represents the X Data array.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166176				0	lv	\<emph\>NewDataX\</emph\> (optional) represents the array of the X data, which are used for recalculating values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166196				0	lv	\<emph\>LinearType\</emph\>(Optional). If LinearType = 0, then lines will be calculated through the zero point. Otherwise, offset lines will also be calculated. The default is LinearType <> 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D2F				0	lv	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
