helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3148502				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZEITWERT\"\>TIMEVALUE returns the internal time number from a text enclosed by quotes and which may show a possible time entry format.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3150794				0	lv	The internal number indicated as a decimal is the result of the date system used under $[officename] to calculate date entries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id011920090347118				0	lv	If the text string also includes a year, month, or day, TIMEVALUE only returns the fractional part of the conversion.				20200411 15:09:53
