helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149519	158			0	lv	            \<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of objects in each permutation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151382				0	lv	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153949				0	lv	How often can 2 objects be selected from a total of 11 objects?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	161			0	lv	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PERMUTATIONA(11;2)\</item\> returns 121.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150622	162			0	lv	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PERMUTATIONA(6;3)\</item\> returns 216. There are 216 different possibilities to put a sequence of 3 playing cards together out of six playing cards if every card is returned before the next one is drawn.				20200411 15:09:53
