helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147478				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCOTHYP\"\>Returns the inverse hyperbolic cotangent of the given number.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152585				0	lv	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172				0	lv	ACOTH(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146155				0	lv	 This function returns the inverse hyperbolic cotangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic cotangent is Number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5818659				0	lv	An error results if Number is between -1 and 1 inclusive.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083452				0	lv	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150608				0	lv	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOTH(1.1)\</item\> returns inverse hyperbolic cotangent of 1.1, approximately 1.52226.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145084				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>ASIN function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
