helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150882				0	lv	ASINH(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147621	104			0	lv	 This function returns the inverse hyperbolic sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic sine is Number. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153212				0	lv	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156120				0	lv	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASINH(-90)\</item\> returns approximately -5.1929877.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id4808496				0	lv	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASINH(SINH(4))\</item\> returns 4.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155996				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>ATAN function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155996				0	lv	ATAN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149985				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCTAN\"\>Returns the inverse trigonometric tangent of a number.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151294				0	lv	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150261				0	lv	ATAN(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147267				0	lv	 This function returns the inverse trigonometric tangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose tangent is Number. The angle returned is between -PI/2 and PI/2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6293527				0	lv	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154054				0	lv	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143229				0	lv	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ATAN(1)\</item\> returns 0.785398163397448 (PI/4 radians).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8746299				0	lv	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ATAN(1))\</item\> returns 45. The tangent of 45 degrees is 1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153983				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>ATAN2 function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153983				0	lv	ATAN2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154297				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCTAN2\"\>Returns the inverse trigonometric tangent of the specified x and y coordinates.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149758				0	lv	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156013				0	lv	ATAN2(NumberX; NumberY)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	lv	\<emph\>NumberX\</emph\> is the value of the x coordinate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152798				0	lv	\<emph\>NumberY\</emph\> is the value of the y coordinate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5036164				0	lv	ATAN2 returns the inverse trigonometric tangent, that is, the angle (in radians) between the x-axis and a line from point NumberX, NumberY to the origin. The angle returned is between -PI and PI.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3001800				0	lv	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145663				0	lv	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154692				0	lv	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ATAN2(20;20)\</item\> returns 0.785398163397448 (PI/4 radians).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1477095				0	lv	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ATAN2(12.3;12.3))\</item\> returns 45. The tangent of 45 degrees is 1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155398				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>ATANH function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
