helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	lv	 Returns the (trigonometric) cosine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id831019				0	lv	To return the cosine of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153579				0	lv	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147240				0	lv	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COS(PI()/2)\</item\> returns 0, the cosine of PI/2 radians.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147516				0	lv	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COS(RADIANS(60))\</item\> returns 0.5, the cosine of 60 degrees.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154277				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>COSH function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
