helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442				0	lv	\<variable id=\"join_objects3d\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/join_objects3d.xhp\" name=\"Assembling 3D Objects\"\>Assembling 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	lv	3D objects that each form a 3D scene can be combined into a single 3D scene.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042				0	lv	To combine 3D objects:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	lv	Insert a 3D object from the \<emph\>3D Objects\</emph\> toolbar (for example, a cube).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	lv	Insert a second slightly larger 3D object (for example, a sphere).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	lv	Select the second 3D object (sphere) and choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211				0	lv	Double-click the first object (cube) to enter its group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>. Both objects are now part of the same group. If you want, you can edit the individual objects or change their position within the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376				0	lv	Double-click outside the group to exit the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	lv	You cannot intersect or subtract 3D objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154537				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10090000.xhp\" name=\"Objects in 3D\"\>Objects in 3D\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Combining Objects and Constructing Shapes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156443				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>combining; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>connecting; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; combining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>intersecting draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>polygons; intersecting/subtracting/merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subtracting polygons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>constructing shapes\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156443	64			0	lv	\<variable id=\"combine_etc\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/combine_etc.xhp\" name=\"Combining Objects and Constructing Shapes\"\>Combining Objects and Constructing Shapes\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149020	65			0	lv	Combined drawing objects act as grouped objects, except that you cannot enter the group to edit the individual objects. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	lv	You can only combine 2D objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150344				0	lv	To combine 2D objects:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	lv	Select two or more 2D objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Modify - Combine\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978				0	lv	Unlike groups, a combined object takes on the properties of the lowermost object in the stacking order. You can split apart combined objects, but the original object properties are lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155088				0	lv	When you combine objects, holes appear where the objects overlap.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	lv	 \<image id=\"img_id3157978\" src=\"res/helpimg/kombi1.png\" width=\"8.3646inch\" height=\"2.5inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3157978\"\>Illustration for combining objects\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153249				0	lv	In the illustration, the uncombined objects are on the left and the combined objects on the right.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159229				0	lv	Constructing Shapes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150049				0	lv	You can construct shapes by applying the \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13180000.xhp\" name=\"Shapes\"\>\<emph\>Shapes\</emph\>\</link\> \<emph\>- Merge, Subtract and Intersect\</emph\> commands to two or more drawing objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147403				0	lv	Shape commands only work on 2D objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150539				0	lv	Constructed shapes take on the properties of the lowermost object in the stacking order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156402				0	lv	To construct a shape:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3157874				0	lv	Select two or more 2D objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Modify - Shapes\</emph\> and one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145829	91			0	lv	 \<emph\>Merge\</emph\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154680	92			0	lv	 \<emph\>Subtract\</emph\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153034				0	lv	 \<emph\>Intersect\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145144				0	lv	Shape Commands				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	lv	In the following illustrations, the original objects are on the left and the modified shapes on the right.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149950				0	lv	Shapes - Merge				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148585				0	lv	 \<image id=\"img_id3145593\" src=\"res/helpimg/formvers.png\" width=\"3.4791inch\" height=\"1.3126inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145593\"\>Illustration for merging shapes\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150001				0	lv	Adds the area of the selected objects to the area of the lowermost object in the stacking order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153002				0	lv	Shapes - Subtract				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150338				0	lv	 \<image id=\"img_id3154505\" src=\"res/helpimg/formsubt.png\" width=\"3.4689inch\" height=\"1.3126inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154505\"\>Illustration for subtracting shapes\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150022				0	lv	Subtracts the area of the selected objects from the area of the lowermost object in the stacking order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147370				0	lv	Shapes - Intersect				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150570				0	lv	 \<image id=\"img_id3150658\" src=\"res/helpimg/formschn.png\" width=\"3.4272inch\" height=\"1.302inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150658\"\>Illustration for intersecting shapes\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3157972				0	lv	The overlapping area of the selected objects creates the new shape.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020				0	lv	The area outside the overlap is removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Rotating Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>rotating; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; rotating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot points of draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>skewing draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	lv	\<variable id=\"rotate_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/rotate_object.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Objects\"\>Rotating Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	lv	You can rotate an object around its default pivot point (center point) or a pivot point that you designate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3154729\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectrotatemode.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154729\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	lv	Select the object you want to rotate. On the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> toolbar in $[officename] Draw or on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar in $[officename] Impress, click the \<emph\>Rotate\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149021				0	lv	Move the pointer to a corner handle so that the pointer changes to a rotate symbol. Drag the handle to rotate the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id0930200803002335				0	lv	Hold down the Shift key to restrict the rotation to multiples of 15 degrees.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id0930200803002463				0	lv	Right-click the object to open the context menu. Choose Position and Size - Rotation to enter an exact rotation value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3154023\" src=\"res/helpimg/rotate.png\" width=\"5.424cm\" height=\"3.916cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154023\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3166424				0	lv	To change the pivot point, drag the small circle in the center of the object to a new location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	lv	To skew the object vertically or horizontally, drag one of the side handles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Adding Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153144				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying;text from other documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pasting;text from other documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>legends; drawings\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153144				0	lv	\<variable id=\"text_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/text_enter.xhp\" name=\"Adding Text\"\>Adding Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	46			0	lv	There are several types of text you can add to a drawing or presentation: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	lv	Text in a text box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	lv	Text that changes character size to fill the frame size				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	lv	Text that is added to any drawing object by double-clicking the object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10830				0	lv	Text that is copied from a Writer document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	lv	Text that is inserted from a text document or HTML document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202				0	lv	Adding a Text Box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266	49			0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156450\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156450\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and move the mouse pointer to where you want to enter the text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149052				0	lv	Drag a text box to the size you want in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3151194				0	lv	Type or paste your text into the text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	lv	Double-click the text to edit it or to format text properties, such as font size or font color. Click the border of the text box to edit the object properties, such as border color or arranging in front or behind other objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150437				0	lv	Fitting Text to Frames				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146877				0	lv	Create a text box as described in the steps above.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	lv	With the text object selected, choose \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Text\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AF				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> tab page, clear the \<emph\>Fit height to text\</emph\> checkbox, then select the \<emph\>Fit to frame\</emph\> checkbox. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id0610200902133994				0	lv	Now you can resize the text box to change the size and shape of the text characters.				20200411 15:09:53
