helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Defining Different Headers and Footers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155920				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>headers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining; headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>mirrored page layout\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155920				0	lv	\<variable id=\"header_pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Defining Different Headers and Footers\"\>Defining Different Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	lv	You can use different headers and footers on different pages in your document, so long as the pages use different page styles. $[officename] provides several predefined page styles, such as \<emph\>First page\</emph\>, \<emph\>Left page\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right page\</emph\>, or you can create a custom page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147105				0	lv	You can also use the mirrored page layout if you want to add a header to a page style that has different inner and outer page margins. To apply this option to a page style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page\</item\> tab, and in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Layout settings\</item\> area, choose “Mirrored” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page layout\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	lv	For example, you can use page styles to define different headers for even and odd pages in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150929				0	lv	Open a new text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon in the Styles and Formatting window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	lv	Right-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> dialog, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	lv	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Next Style\</item\> box, select "Left Page".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146889				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150714				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, right-click "Left Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150748				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> dialog, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	lv	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147061				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Next Style\</item\> box, select "Right Page".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147086				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	lv	Double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles to apply the style to the current page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145284	43			0	lv	Enter text or graphics in the header for the Left Page style. After the next page is added to your document, enter text or graphics in the header for the Right Page style. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Adding Input Fields				20200411 15:09:53
