helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916	1			0	lv	\<variable id=\"fields_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields_enter.xhp\" name=\"Adding Input Fields\"\>Adding Input Fields\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	lv	An input field is a variable that you can click in a document to open a dialog where you can edit the variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145776				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\> click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	lv	Click “Input field” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154257				0	lv	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and type the text for the variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150708				0	lv	To quickly open all input fields in a document for editing, press Ctrl+Shift+F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153407				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>page styles; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>blank pages with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>empty page with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; even/odd pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>title pages; page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>First Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Left Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>even/odd pages;formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153407				0	lv	\<variable id=\"even_odd_sdw\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/even_odd_sdw.xhp\" name=\"Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\"\>Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154265				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3155876\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_designerdialog.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155876\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	lv	$[officename] can automatically apply alternating page styles on even (left) and odd pages (right) in your document. For example, you can use page styles to display different headers and footers on even and odd pages. The current page style is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the workplace.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id8194219				0	lv	To Set Up Alternating Page Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150526				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	lv	In the list of page styles, right-click "Left Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179				0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145267				0	lv	Select "Right Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	lv	In the list of page styles, right-click "Right Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	lv	Select "Left Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155561				0	lv	Go to the first page in your document, and double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles in the Styles and Formatting window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155588				0	lv	To add a header to one of the page styles, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the header to. In the header frame, type the text that you want to use as the header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147772				0	lv	To add a footer to one of the page styles, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the footer to. In the footer frame, type the text that you want to use as a footer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	lv	If you do not want to have a header or a footer on the title page of your document, apply the "First Page" style to the title page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id888698				0	lv	To Suppress the Printout of Empty Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	lv	If two even or two odd pages directly follow each other in your document, Writer will insert an empty page by default. You can suppress those automatically generated empty pages from printing and from exporting to PDF.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id8147221				0	lv	Remove the check mark from \<emph\>Print automatically inserted blank pages\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Break dialog\"\>Insert Break dialog\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Saving Text Documents in HTML Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>text documents; publishing in HTML\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; creating from text documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>homepage creation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>saving;in HTML format\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	lv	\<variable id=\"send2html\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/send2html.xhp\" name=\"Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\"\>Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149825				0	lv	You can save a $[officename] Writer document in HTML format, so that you can view it in a web browser. If you want, you can associate a page break with a specific heading paragraph style to generate a separate HTML page each time the style appears in the document. $[officename] Writer automatically creates a page containing hyperlinks to each of these pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	lv	When you save a text document in HTML format, any graphics in the document are saved in JPEG format. The name of the HTML document is added as a prefix to the name of the graphic file. The JPEG images are saved in the same folder as the HTML document and are referenced with <IMG> tags in the HTML code.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155868				0	lv	Apply one of the default $[officename] heading paragraph styles, for example, "Heading 1", to the paragraphs where you want to generate a new HTML page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3156100				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create HTML Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles\</item\> box, select the paragraph style that you want to use to generate a new HTML page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3153407				0	lv	Enter a path and a name for the HTML document, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Navigating and Selecting With the Keyboard				20200411 15:09:53
