helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147828				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>objects;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>positioning;objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>anchors;options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>centering;images on HTML pages\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147828				0	lv	\<variable id=\"anchor_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/anchor_object.xhp\" name=\"Positioning Objects\"\>Positioning Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3147251				0	lv	You can use anchors to position an object, graphic, or frame in a document. An anchored item remains in place, or moves when you modify the document. The following anchoring options are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145599				0	lv	Anchoring				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145622				0	lv	Effect				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145650				0	lv	As character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151181				0	lv	Anchors the selected item as a character in the current text. If the height of the selected item is greater than the current font size, the height of the line containing the item is increased.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	lv	To center an image on an HTML page, insert the image, anchor it "as character", then center the paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	lv	To character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151235				0	lv	Anchors the selected item to a character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155071				0	lv	To paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155094				0	lv	Anchors the selected item to the current paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155122				0	lv	To page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155144				0	lv	Anchors the selected item to the current page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	lv	To frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145697				0	lv	Anchors the selected item to the surrounding frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145715				0	lv	When you insert an object, graphic, or frame, an anchor icon appears where the item is anchored. You can position an anchored item by dragging the item to another location. To change the anchoring options of an item, right-click the item, and then choose an option from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Anchor\</item\> submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Adding Line Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
