helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147406				0	lv	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\"\>Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	lv	You can use predefined functions in a formula, and then insert the result of the calculation into a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152901				0	lv	For example, to calculate the mean value of three numbers, do the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	lv	Click in the document where you want to insert the formula, and then press F2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	lv	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\> icon, and choose "Mean" from the Statistical Functions list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	lv	Type the three numbers, separated by vertical slashes (|).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	lv	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>. The result is inserted as a field into the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149823				0	lv	To edit the formula, double-click the field in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
