helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155915				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>Stylist, see Styles and Formatting window\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>templates; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Styles and Formatting window; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating; styles, from selections\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155915				0	lv	\<variable id=\"stylist_update\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_update.xhp\" name=\"Updating Styles From Selections\"\>Updating Styles From Selections\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3149838				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3156107				0	lv	Click the icon of the style category that you want to update.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	lv	In the document, click from where you want to copy the updated style. For example, click a paragraph to which you applied some manual formatting that you want to copy now.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	lv	In the Styles and Formatting window, click the style that you want to update.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	lv	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and choose \<emph\>Update Style\</emph\> from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id0310200910360780				0	lv	Only the manually formatted attributes of the text at the cursor position in the document will be added to the style that is selected in the Styles and Formatting window. Any attributes that were applied as part of a style will not be added to the updated style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3155498				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Creating New Styles From Selections				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155911				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>styles; creating from selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;creating new styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying;styles, from selections\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155911				0	lv	\<variable id=\"stylist_fromselect\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fromselect.xhp\" name=\"Creating New Styles From Selections\"\>Creating New Styles From Selections\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	lv	To Create a New Style From a Manually Formatted Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156097				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	lv	Click the icon of the style category that you want to create.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	lv	Click in the document where you want to copy the style from, for example, in a paragraph that you applied manual formatting to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138				0	lv	Click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Style from Selection\</item\> icon and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Style from Selection\</item\> from the submenu				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	lv	Type a name in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style Name\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154411				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153373				0	lv	To Create a New Style by Drag-And-Drop				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	lv	Click the icon of the style category that you want to create.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154851				0	lv	Select at least one character, or object, in the style that you want to copy. For page and frame styles, select at least one character or object in the page or frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	lv	Drag the character or object to the Styles and Formatting window and release.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	lv	For paragraph and character styles, you can drag-and-drop onto the respective icon in the Styles and Formatting window. You do not need to open that style category in advance.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B5				0	lv	You can also drag-and-drop a frame into the Styles and Formatting window to create a new frame style: Click the frame, wait a moment with the mouse button pressed down, but without moving the mouse, then drag to the Styles and Formatting window and drop the frame onto the Frame Styles icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149988				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	User Defined Borders in Text Documents 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	bm_id6737876				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>borders;for text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;borders in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;table borders in Writer\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;around text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;defining borders\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3614917				0	lv	\<variable id=\"borders\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/borders.xhp\"\>User Defined Borders in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1069368				0	lv	You can apply a variety of different cell borders to selected cells in a Writer table and to the whole table. Other objects in text documents can have user defined borders, too. For example, you can assign borders to page styles, to frames, and to inserted pictures or charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6527298				0	lv	Select the cell or a block of cells in a Writer table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6129947				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table - Table properties\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8141117				0	lv	In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6016418				0	lv	Choose the border options you want to apply and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5282448				0	lv	The options in the \<emph\>Line arrangement\</emph\> area can be used to apply multiple border styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3547166				0	lv	Selection of cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1108432				0	lv	Depending on the selection of cells, the area looks different.				20200411 15:09:53
