helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Rearranging a Document by Using the Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149973				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>headings;rearranging\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rearranging headings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>moving;headings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>demoting heading levels\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>promoting heading levels\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Navigator;heading levels and chapters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>arranging;headings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>outlines;arranging chapters\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149973				0	lv	\<variable id=\"arrange_chapters\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/arrange_chapters.xhp\" name=\"Rearranging a Document by Using the Navigator\"\>Arranging Chapters in the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147795	59			0	lv	You can move headings and subordinate text up and down in a document text by using the Navigator. You can also promote and demote heading levels. To use this feature, format the headings in your document with one of the predefined heading paragraph styles. To use a custom paragraph style for a heading, choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>, select the style in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>box, and then double-click a number in the \<emph\>Levels \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145652	62			0	lv	To quickly move the text cursor to a heading in the document, double-click the heading in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155461				0	lv	To dock the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, drag the title bar to the edge of the workspace. To undock the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, double-click its frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151184				0	lv	To Move a Heading Up or Down in the Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id0915200809400790				0	lv	Ensure that all heading levels are shown in the Navigator. By default all levels are shown. See steps below how to change the heading levels that are shown.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151206	71			0	lv	On the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>, click the\<emph\> Navigator\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id5211883\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_navigator.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5211883\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151238	72			0	lv	On the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Content View\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156338\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20234.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156338\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155089				0	lv	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	63			0	lv	Drag a heading to a new location in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155139	75			0	lv	Click a heading in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list, and then click the \<emph\>Promote Chapter\</emph\>\<image id=\"img_id4217546\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20174.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4217546\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or \<emph\>Demote Chapter \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id6505788\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20171.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6505788\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145758	64			0	lv	To move the heading without the subordinate text, hold down Ctrl while you drag or click the \<emph\>Promote Chapter \</emph\>or \<emph\>Demote Chapter \</emph\>icons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155402				0	lv	To Promote or Demote the Level of a Heading				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155424	77			0	lv	Select the heading in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081C				0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Promote Level \</emph\>\<image id=\"img_id5564488\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20172.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5564488\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or \<emph\>Demote Level \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id3159363\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20173.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159363\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155525				0	lv	To Change the Number of Heading Levels That Are Displayed				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151352	79			0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Heading Levels Shown \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id3151310\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20236.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151310\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>, and then select a number from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Inserting a Scanned Image				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156017				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>inserting;scanned images\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; scanning\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scanning pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156017				0	lv	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_scan\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_scan.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Scanned Image\"\>Inserting a Scanned Image\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	lv	To insert a scanned image, the scanner must be connected to your system and the scanner software drivers must be installed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182	3			0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>The scanner must support the TWAIN standard. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>The scanner must support the SANE standard.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3155915				0	lv	Click in the document where you want to insert the scanned image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	lv	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Picture - Scan\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Picture - Scan\</emph\>\</link\>, and choose the scanning source from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	lv	Follow the scanning instructions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Conditional Text for Page Counts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153108				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>page counts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text;page counts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153108				0	lv	\<variable id=\"conditional_text2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text2.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text for Page Counts\"\>Conditional Text for Page Counts\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156228				0	lv	You can create a conditional text field that displays the word "pages" instead of "page" in conjunction with a page count field if your document contains more than one page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	lv	Place the cursor in your document where you want to insert the page count.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</item\>, and then enter a space.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166				0	lv	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256				0	lv	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page > 1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145280				0	lv	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Pages\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Then\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145305				0	lv	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Else\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Turning Off AutoCorrect 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154250				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>turning off automatic correction\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text;turning off automatic correction\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>uppercase;changing to lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters after periods\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>quotation marks;changing automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>words;automatic replacement on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;automatic drawing on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>underlining;quick\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders; automatic drawing on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic changes on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changes;automatic\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;turning off\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147812				0	lv	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Turning Off AutoFormat and AutoCorrect\"\>Turning Off AutoCorrect\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833	2			0	lv	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	lv	To quickly undo an automatic correction or completion, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	lv	To turn off most AutoCorrect features, remove the check mark from the menu \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect - While Typing\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147251				0	lv	To Remove a Word from the AutoCorrect List				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147274				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596				0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145620				0	lv	In the \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\> list, select the word pair that you want to remove.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145645				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145668				0	lv	To Stop Replacing Quotation Marks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3151196				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3151220				0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Localized Options\</emph\> tab				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	lv	Clear the "Replace" check box(es).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155076				0	lv	To Stop Capitalizing the First Letter of a Sentence				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155099	10			0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155123				0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155148				0	lv	Clear the "Capitalize first letter of every sentence" check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155401				0	lv	To Stop Drawing a Line When You Type Three Identical Characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155415				0	lv	$[officename] automatically draws a line when you type three of the following characters and press Enter: - _ = * ~ #				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155439				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155463				0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155488				0	lv	Clear the "Apply border" check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Checking Spelling and Grammar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149684				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; checking text documents manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>checking spelling;manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>grammar checker\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149684				0	lv	\<variable id=\"spellcheck_dialog\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/spellcheck_dialog.xhp\" name=\"Checking Spelling and Grammar\"\>Checking Spelling and Grammar\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149814				0	lv	You can manually check the spelling and grammar of a text selection or the entire document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id0525200902184476				0	lv	To check the spelling and the grammar of a text, the appropriate dictionaries must be installed. For many languages three different dictionaries exist: a spellchecker, a hyphenation dictionary, and a thesaurus. Each dictionary covers one language only. Grammar checkers can be downloaded and installed as extensions. See the \<link href=\"https://extensions.openoffice.org/dictionary\"\>extensions web page\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149828				0	lv	The spellcheck starts at the current cursor position, or at the beginning of the text selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155859				0	lv	Click in the document, or select the text that you want to check.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Spelling and Grammar\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104				0	lv	When a possible spelling error is encountered, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Spellcheck\</item\> dialog opens and $[officename] offers some suggested corrections.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149861				0	lv	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3145099				0	lv	To accept a correction, click the suggestion, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	lv	Edit the sentence in the upper text box, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	lv	To add the unknown word to a user-defined dictionary, click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3147107				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06010000.xhp\" name=\"Spellcheck dialog\"\>Spelling and Grammar dialog\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id9625843				0	lv	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Adding_More_Languages\"\>Wiki page: Adding more languages\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id1683706				0	lv	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Spellchecking_in_More_Languages\"\>Wiki page: Multiple language spellchecking\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Inserting a Fixed or Variable Date Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	bm_id5111545				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>inserting;date fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dates;inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date fields;fixed/variable\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fixed dates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variable dates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155165				0	lv	\<variable id=\"fields_date\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields_date.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Fixed or Variable Date Field\"\>Inserting a Fixed or Variable Date Field\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	lv	You can insert the current date as a field that updates each time you open the document, or as a field that does not update.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147679				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Document\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	lv	Click “Date” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list and do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	lv	To insert the date as a field that updates each time you open the document, click ”Date” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Select\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3154241				0	lv	To insert the date as a field that does not update, click “Date (fixed)” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Select\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Indenting Paragraphs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155869				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>formatting; indenting paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>indents;in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; indents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hanging indents in paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right indents in paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines of text; indents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;indents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	hd_id129398				0	lv	\<variable id=\"indenting\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indenting.xhp\"\>Indenting Paragraphs\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id5589159				0	lv	To change the measurement units, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</item\>, and then select a new measurement unit in the Settings area. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id9936216				0	lv	You can change the indents for the current paragraph, or for all selected paragraphs, or for a Paragraph Style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id7953123				0	lv	You can also \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\" name=\"ruler\"\>set indents using the ruler\</link\>. To display the ruler, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Ruler\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</item\> to change the indents for the current paragraph or for all selected paragraphs. You can also \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\" name=\"ruler\"\>set indents using the ruler\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id1631824				0	lv	Right-click a paragraph and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit Paragraph Style - Indents & Spacing\</item\> to change the indents for all paragraphs that have the same Paragraph Style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id7271645				0	lv	Indents are calculated with respect to the left and right page margins. If you want the paragraph to extend into the page margin, enter a negative number. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id2136295				0	lv	The indents are different regarding the writing direction. For example, look at the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before text \</item\>indent value in left-to-right languages. The left edge of the paragraph is indented with respect to the left page margin. In right-to-left languages, the right edge of the paragraph is indented with respect to the right page margin.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	lv	For a hanging indent, enter a positive value for \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before text\</item\> and a negative value for \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>First line\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\"\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155919				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>running titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>floating titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headers; chapter information\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919				0	lv	\<variable id=\"header_with_chapter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_chapter.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\"\>Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	lv	Before you can insert chapter information into a header or footer, you must first set the outline numbering options for the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154244				0	lv	To Create a Paragraph Style for Chapter Titles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155874				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155898				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> box, select the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles, for example, "Heading 1".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	lv	Select the numbering style for the chapter titles in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number\</item\> box, for example, "1,2,3...".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150219				0	lv	Type "Chapter" followed by a space in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150245				0	lv	Enter a space in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>After\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150949				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150505				0	lv	To Insert the Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150527				0	lv	Apply the paragraph style that you defined for chapter titles to the chapter headings in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153729				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer\</item\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153762				0	lv	Click in the header or footer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146863				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Document\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153175				0	lv	Click "Chapter" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list and "Chapter number and name" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147065				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147095				0	lv	The header on every page that uses the current page style automatically displays the chapter name and number.				20200411 15:09:53
