helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145246				0	lv	\<variable id=\"globaldoc_howtos\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/globaldoc_howtos.xhp\"\>Working with Master Documents and Subdocuments\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id1522873				0	lv	A master document lets you manage large documents, such as a book with many chapters. The master document can be seen as a container for individual \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer files. The individual files are called subdocuments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	lv	To Create a Master Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	lv	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Master Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	lv	Open an existing document and choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create Master Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	lv	If you are creating a new master document, the first entry in the Navigator should be a \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text\</item\> entry. Type an introduction or enter some text. This ensures that after having edited an existing style in the master document, you see the changed style when viewing the subdocuments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145114				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Navigator\</item\> for master documents (should open automatically, else press F5 to open), click and hold the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> icon, and do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3156240				0	lv	To insert an existing file as a subdocument, choose \<emph\>File\</emph\>, locate the file that you want to include, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145405				0	lv	To create a new subdocument, choose \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, type a name for the file, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8550981				0	lv	To insert some text between subdocuments, choose \<emph\>Text\</emph\>. Then type the text. You cannot insert text next to an existing text entry in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153382				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	lv	To Edit a Master Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	lv	Use the Navigator for rearranging and editing the subdocuments in a master document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	lv	To open a subdocument for editing, double-click the name of the subdocument in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155931				0	lv	To remove a subdocument from the master document, right-click the subdocument in the Navigator list and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. The subdocument file is not deleted, only the entry in the Navigator is removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148677				0	lv	To add text to a master document, right-click an item in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Text\</emph\>. A text section is inserted before the selected item in the master document where you can type the text that you want. You cannot insert text next to an existing text entry in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149982				0	lv	To reorder the subdocuments in a master document, drag a subdocument to a new location in the Navigator list. You can also select a subdocument in the list, and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move down\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move up\</item\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153022				0	lv	To add an index, such as a table of contents, right-click in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3148959\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20246.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148959\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	lv	To update an index in a master document, select the index in the Navigator, and then click the \<emph\>Update\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C40				0	lv	When you insert an object like a frame or a picture into a master document, do not anchor the object "to page". Instead, set the anchor "to paragraph" on the \<emph\>Format - (Object type) - Type\</emph\> tab page, and then set the object's position relative to "Entire Page" in the \<emph\>Horizontal\</emph\> and \<emph\>Vertical\</emph\> list boxes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153656				0	lv	To Start Each Subdocument on a New Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	lv	Ensure that each subdocument starts with a heading that uses the same paragraph style, for example "Heading 1".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	lv	In the master document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153907				0	lv	Right-click "Heading 1" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	lv	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Flow\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149770				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Breaks\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>, and then select “Page” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	lv	If you want each subdocument to start on an odd page, select \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>, and select "Right page" in the box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145205				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228				0	lv	To Export a Master Document as a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Text Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150315				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Export\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148580				0	lv	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> list, select a text document file format and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8371227				0	lv	The subdocuments will be exported as sections. Use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Sections\</item\> to unprotect and remove sections, if you prefer a plain text document without sections.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Thesaurus				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145576				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>thesaurus; related words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>related words in thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spelling in thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dictionaries; thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lexicon, see thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>synonyms in thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>searching;synonyms\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145576				0	lv	\<variable id=\"using_thesaurus\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_thesaurus.xhp\" name=\"Thesaurus\"\>Thesaurus\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3149820				0	lv	You can use the thesaurus to look up synonyms or related terms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3155920				0	lv	Click in the word that you want to look up or replace.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3155867				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Language - Thesaurus\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F7.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3149848				0	lv	In the Alternatives list, click an entry to copy that related term to the "Replace with" text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	lv	Optionally double-click an entry to look up related terms for that entry. On your keyboard, you can also press the arrow up or down keys to select an entry. Then press Return to replace, or press the spacebar to look up.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3156263				0	lv	Initially, the thesaurus uses the language of the selected word in the document, if a thesaurus library for that language is installed. The title bar of the Thesaurus dialog displays the language in use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3145113				0	lv	To look up the word in a different language, click the Language button, and select one of the installed thesaurus languages. A thesaurus library may not be available for all installed languages. You can install languages with a thesaurus library from the \<link href=\"https://extensions.openoffice.org/\"\>Extensions\</link\> web page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3196263				0	lv	If a thesaurus library is installed for the language of a word, the context menu of the word shows a Synonyms submenu. Select any of the terms from the submenu to replace the word.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3154392				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06020000.xhp\" name=\"Thesaurus\"\>Thesaurus\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147688				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>user-defined dictionaries; removing words from\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>custom dictionaries; removing words from\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;words in user-defined dictionaries\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147688				0	lv	\<variable id=\"delete_from_dict\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/delete_from_dict.xhp\" name=\"Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary\"\>Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Writing Aids\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3151391				0	lv	Select the user-defined dictionary that you want to edit in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>User-defined\</item\> list, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	lv	Select the word that you want to delete in the \<emph\>Word\</emph\> list, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Merging and Splitting Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147240				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>cells; merging/splitting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; merging cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell merges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>splitting cells;by menu command\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id6618243				0	lv	\<variable id=\"table_cellmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_cellmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging and Splitting Cells\"\>Merging and Splitting Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id1211890				0	lv	You can select adjacent cells, then merge them into a single cell. Conversely, you can take a large cell and divide it into individual cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id3463850				0	lv	To Merge Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id5708792				0	lv	Select the adjacent cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id6301461				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Table - Merge Cells\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id9156468				0	lv	To Split Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3415936				0	lv	Place the cursor in the cell to be split.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id4044312				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Table - Split Cells\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id634174				0	lv	A dialog allows you to split the cell into two or more cells, horizontally or vertically.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Inserting Graphics				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154922				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>text; inserting pictures in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting options\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154922				0	lv	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics\"\>Inserting Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149695				0	lv	There are several ways to insert a graphic object in a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Preventing Hyphenation of Specific Words				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>hyphenation;preventing for specific words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>words;wrapping/not wrapping in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>switching off;hyphenation for specific words\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	lv	\<variable id=\"hyphen_prevent\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyphen_prevent.xhp\" name=\"Preventing Hyphenation of Specific Words\"\>Preventing Hyphenation of Specific Words\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id5640125				0	lv	If your text is \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_hyphen.xhp\"\>automatically hyphenated\</link\> and certain hyphenated words look ugly, or if you want specific words never to be hyphenated you can switch off hyphenation for those words:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3153634	40			0	lv	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Writing Aids\</emph\>            				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3153658	41			0	lv	Select a dictionary in the \<emph\>User-defined dictionary \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125				0	lv	If the list is empty, click \<emph\>New\</emph\> to create a dictionary.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150218	42			0	lv	In the\<emph\> Word\</emph\> box, type the word you want to exclude from hyphenation, followed by an equal sign (=), for example, "pretentious=".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150247				0	lv	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147036	29			0	lv	To quickly exclude a word from hyphenation, select the word, choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Font \</emph\>tab, and select "None" in the \<emph\>Language \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id0302200910262761				0	lv	Some words contain special characters that %PRODUCTNAME treats as a hyphen. If you do not want such words to be hyphenated, you can insert a special code that prevents hyphenation at the position where the special code is inserted. Proceed as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id0302200910262850				0	lv	Enable the special features of complex text layout (CTL) languages: Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\> and check \<emph\>Enabled for complex text layout (CTL)\</emph\>. Click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id0302200910262837				0	lv	Position the cursor at the place where no hyphenation should occur.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id0302200910262867				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Formatting Mark - No-width no break\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id0302200910572128				0	lv	Once the special character is inserted, you might disable CTL again. Support of CTL was only necessary to insert the special character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145819				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>pages; continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>next page number in footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page numbers; continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145819				0	lv	\<variable id=\"footer_nextpage\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footer_nextpage.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages\"\>Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154242				0	lv	You can easily insert the page number of the next page in a footer by using a field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	lv	The page number is only displayed if the following page exists.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\> and select the page style that you want to add the footer to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109				0	lv	Place the cursor in the footer and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147134				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>Document\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150955				0	lv	Click 'Page' in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list and 'Next page' in the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	lv	Click a numbering style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	lv	If you select 'Text' in the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, only the text that you enter in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box is displayed in the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150727				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> to insert the field with the page number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Inserting Page Numbers in Footers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155624				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>footers; with page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages; numbers and count of\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page numbers; footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering;pages\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155624				0	lv	\<variable id=\"footer_pagenumber\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footer_pagenumber.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\"\>Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id8230842				0	lv	You can easily insert a page number field in the footer of your document. You can also add a page count to the footer, for example, in the form "Page 9 of 12"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id7867366				0	lv	To Insert a Page Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\> and select the page style that you want to add the footer to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3153155				0	lv	If you want, you can align the page number field as you would text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id2988677				0	lv	To Additionally Add a Page Count				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3155532				0	lv	Click in front of the page number field, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page\</item\> and enter a space; click after the field, enter a space and then type \<item type=\"literal\"\>of\</item\> and enter another space.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3155554				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Page Numbers 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id5918759				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>page numbers;inserting/defining/formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles;page numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>starting page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;starting page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id413830				0	lv	\<variable id=\"pagenumbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>Page Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1617175				0	lv	In Writer, a page number is a field that you can insert into your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id6091494				0	lv	To Insert Page Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id8611102				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\> to insert a page number at the current cursor position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6604510				0	lv	If you see the text "Page number" instead of the number, choose \<emph\>View - Field names\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2678914				0	lv	However, these fields will change position when you add or remove text. So it is best to insert the page number field into a header or footer that has the same position and that is repeated on every page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id614642				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header - (name of page style)\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer - (name of page style)\</item\> to add a header or footer to all pages with the current page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id2551652				0	lv	To Start With a Defined Page Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6111941				0	lv	Now you want some more control on page numbers. You are writing a text document that should start with page number 12.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5757621				0	lv	Click into the first paragraph of your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2632831				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Text flow\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4395275				0	lv	In the Breaks area, enable \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. Enable \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\> just to be able to set the new \<emph\>Page number\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1654408				0	lv	The new page number is an attribute of the first paragraph of the page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id7519150				0	lv	To Format the Page Number Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9029206				0	lv	You want roman page numbers running i, ii, iii, iv, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3032319				0	lv	Double-click directly before the page number field. You see the \<emph\>Edit Fields\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9139378				0	lv	Select a number format and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5051728				0	lv	Using Different Page Number Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1558885				0	lv	You need some pages with the roman numbering style, followed by the remaining pages in another style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1541184				0	lv	In Writer, you will need different page styles. The first page style has a footer with a page number field formatted for roman numbers. The following page style has a footer with a page number field formatted in another look.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id18616				0	lv	Both page styles must be separated by a page break. In Writer, you can have automatic page breaks and manually inserted page breaks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	lv	An \<emph\>automatic page break\</emph\> appears at the end of a page when the page style has a different "next style".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4569231				0	lv	For example, the "First Page" page style has "Default" as the next style. To see this, you may press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles and Formatting\</item\> window, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> icon, right-click the First Page entry. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify\</item\> from the context menu. On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab, you can see the "next style".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	lv	A \<emph\>manually inserted page break\</emph\> can be applied without or with a change of page styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	lv	If you just press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>, you apply a page break without a change of styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5947141				0	lv	If you choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual break\</emph\>, you can insert a page break without or with a change of style or with a change of page number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	lv	It depends on your document what is best: to use a manually inserted page break between page styles, or to use an automatic change. If you just need one title page with a different style than the other pages, you can use the automatic method:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	lv	To Apply a Different Page Style to the First Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	lv	Click into the first page of your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4313791				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	lv	Double-click the "First Page" style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	lv	Now your title page has the style "First Page", and the next pages automatically have the "Default" style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id399182				0	lv	You can now for example insert a footer for the "Default" page atyle only, or insert footers in both page styles, but with differently formatted page number fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5298318				0	lv	To Apply a Manually Inserted Page Style Change				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	lv	Click at the start of the first paragraph on the page where a different page style will be applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>. You see the \<emph\>Insert Break\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> list box, select a page style. You may set a new page number, too. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	lv	The selected page style will be used from the current paragraph to the next page break with style. You may need to create the new page style first.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Changing Page Backgrounds				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	bm_id8431653				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>backgrounds; different pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;page backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	lv	\<variable id=\"pagebackground\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp\"\>Changing Page Background\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10812				0	lv	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the background of the pages in a document. For example, to change the page background of one or more pages in a document to a watermark, you need to create a page style that uses the watermark background, and then apply the page style to the pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10820				0	lv	To Change the Page Background				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10827				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	lv	In the list of page styles, right-click an item, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083F				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084B				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10855				0	lv	To only apply the new page style to a single page, select "Default".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10859				0	lv	To apply the new page style to all subsequent pages, select the name of the new page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1085F				0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10867				0	lv	In the list box at the top, select whether you want a solid color or a graphic. Then select your options from the tab page. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1086B				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087A				0	lv	To Change the Page Background of All Pages in a Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087E				0	lv	Before you begin, ensure that you have created a page style that uses a page background. See \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp#define\"\>To Change the Page Background\</link\> for details.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10892				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089A				0	lv	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	lv	Double-click the page style that uses the page background that you want to apply.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	lv	To Use Different Page Backgrounds in the Same Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A9				0	lv	Before you begin, ensure that you have created a page style that uses a page background. See \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp#define\"\>To Change the Page Background\</link\> for details.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BD				0	lv	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph where you want to change the page background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C1				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C9				0	lv	Select \<emph\>Page break\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D1				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> box, select a page style that uses the page background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DB				0	lv	To change the background of the current page only, select a page style where the Next Style option is set to "Default".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DF				0	lv	To change the background of the current and subsequent pages, select a page style where the Next Style option is set to the name of the page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	lv	If you want to change the page background later on in the document, repeat steps 1 to 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E8				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156108				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>cells; enlarging and reducing in text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table cells; enlarging/reducing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard; resizing rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;rows and columns in text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>enlarging columns,cells and table rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reducing rows and columns in text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; resizing/juxtaposing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>juxtaposing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>heights of table rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>widths of table columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows;resizing in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;resizing in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column widths in tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156108				0	lv	\<variable id=\"table_sizing\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_sizing.xhp\" name=\"Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table\"\>Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	lv	You can resize the width of table cells and columns, as well as change the height of table rows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149615				0	lv	\<image id=\"img_id3149622\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_optimizetable.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149622\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3146497				0	lv	You can also distribute rows and columns evenly using the icons on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Optimize\</item\> toolbar on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table\</item\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145109				0	lv	Changing the Width of Columns and Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149574				0	lv	To Change the Width of a Column				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149587				0	lv	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156246				0	lv	Rest the mouse pointer over the column dividing line until the pointer becomes a separator icon, and then drag the line to a new location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3145390				0	lv	Rest the mouse pointer over the column dividing line on the ruler until the pointer becomes a separator icon, and then drag the line to a new location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id0918200811260957				0	lv	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and then click and drag a line to scale all cells right or above the line proportionally.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3145411				0	lv	Place the cursor in a cell in the column, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364				0	lv	To increase the distance from the left edge of the page to the edge of the table, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift, and then press the right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3155891				0	lv	You can specify the behavior for the arrow keys by choosing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\> - \</emph\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</emph\>, and selecting the options that you want in the \<emph\>Keyboard handling\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149993				0	lv	To Change the Width of a Cell				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3148676				0	lv	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press the left or the right arrow key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153014				0	lv	Changing the Height of a Row				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153035				0	lv	To change the height of a row, place the cursor in a cell in the row, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, and then press the up or the down arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id8478041				0	lv	Resizing a Whole Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3358867				0	lv	To change the width and height of a table, do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id5366679				0	lv	Click inside the table. In the rulers, drag the border between the white and the gray area to resize the table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id1279030				0	lv	Click inside the table. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table - Table Properties\</item\> to open a dialog and set the properties to the numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id5009308				0	lv	To wrap text to the sides of a table, and to arrange two tables next to another, you must insert the tables into a frame. Click inside the table, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A twice to select the whole table, then choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id4190496				0	lv	Tables within HTML pages do not offer the full range of properties and commands as tables in OpenDocument format.				20200411 15:09:53
