helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156383				0	lv	\<variable id=\"number_date_conv\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/number_date_conv.xhp\" name=\"Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables\"\>Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155179				0	lv	$[officename] can automatically format dates that you have entered into a table, according to the regional settings specified in your operating system.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3149966				0	lv	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155919				0	lv	Right-click in a table cell and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number recognition\</item\>. When this feature is on, a check mark is displayed in front of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number recognition\</item\> command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155527				0	lv	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</item\>, and select or clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number recognition\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	lv	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040500.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Table\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149637				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; removing/interrupting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullet lists; interrupting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;removing/interrupting numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>interrupting numbered lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;starting numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149637				0	lv	\<variable id=\"numbering_paras\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_paras.xhp\" name=\"Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\"\>Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3145092				0	lv	You can remove the numbering from a paragraph in a numbered list or change the number that a numbered list starts with.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id2172612				0	lv	If you want numbered headings, use the \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> menu command to assign a numbering to a paragraph style. Do not use the Numbering icon on the Formatting toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145107				0	lv	To Remove the Number From a Paragraph in a Numbered List				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3156248				0	lv	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph that you want to remove the numbering from.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153366				0	lv	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153390				0	lv	To remove the number while preserving the indent of the paragraph, press the Backspace key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	lv	To remove the number and the indent of the paragraph, click the \<emph\>Numbering on/off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar. If you save the document in HTML format, a separate numbered list is created for the numbered paragraphs that follow the current paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154856				0	lv	To Change the Number That a Numbered List Starts With				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155877				0	lv	Click anywhere in the numbered list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3148691	22			0	lv	Enter the number you want the list to start with in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Start \</item\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>at\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3147116				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
