helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Indexes Covering Several Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;multiple documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>master documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	lv	\<variable id=\"indices_multidoc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_multidoc.xhp\" name=\"Indexes Covering Several Documents\"\>Indexes Covering Several Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	lv	There are several ways to create an index that spans several documents:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	lv	Create an \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120210.xhp\" name=\"index in each individual document\"\>index in each individual document\</link\>, copy and paste the indexes into a single document, and then edit them.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147118				0	lv	Select each index, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Section\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>\</link\>, and then enter a name for the index. In a separate document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\>, click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>), and then locate and insert a named index section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150230				0	lv	Create a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010001.xhp\" name=\"master document\"\>master document\</link\>, add as subdocuments the files that you want to include in the index, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Templates and Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153396				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>formatting styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>organizing; templates (guide)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>templates; organizing (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153396				0	lv	\<variable id=\"templates_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/templates_styles.xhp\" name=\"Templates and Styles\"\>Templates and Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	lv	A template is a document that contains specific formatting styles, graphics, tables, objects, and other information. A template is used as the basis for creating other documents. For example, you can define paragraph and character styles in a document, save the document as a template, and then use the template to create a new document with the same styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149957				0	lv	Unless you specify otherwise, every new $[officename] text document is based on the default template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149974				0	lv	$[officename] has a number of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"predefined templates\"\>predefined templates\</link\> that you can use to create different types or text documents, such as business letters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149613				0	lv	Viewing and Organizing Styles in Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	lv	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Template Management\"\>Template Management\</link\> dialog to copy styles from one document to another.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153377				0	lv	To copy a style, drag it to another template or document.				20200411 15:09:53
