helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3154254	11			0	lv	You can prevent AutoCorrect from correcting specific abbreviations or words that have mixed capital letters and lowercase letters. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3155576				0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Exceptions\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147762				0	lv	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147786	19			0	lv	Type the abbreviation followed by a period in the \<emph\>Abbreviations (no subsequent capital) \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812	20			0	lv	Type the word in the \<emph\>Words with TWo INitial CApitals \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3144875	17			0	lv	To quickly undo an AutoCorrect replacement, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. This also adds the word or abbreviation that you typed to the AutoCorrect exceptions list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147684				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>captions; adding chapter numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; captioning automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering; captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic numbering;of objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter numbers in captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;chapter numbers in captions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147684				0	lv	\<variable id=\"captions_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\"\>Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147395				0	lv	You can include chapter numbers in captions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147408				0	lv	Ensure that the text in your document is organized by chapters, and that the chapter titles and, if you want, the section titles, use one of the predefined heading paragraph styles. You must also assign a numbering option to the heading paragraph styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154249				0	lv	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150527	19			0	lv	Select a caption title from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Category\</item\> box, and select a numbering style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> box. \<br/\>You also can enter a caption text in this dialog. If you want, enter text in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Caption\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166				0	lv	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> box, select the number of heading levels to include in the chapter number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155553				0	lv	Type the character that you want to separate the chapter number(s) from the caption number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Separator\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	lv	In the \<emph\>Caption\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226				0	lv	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, or table. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145567				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01041100.xhp\" name=\"Caption dialog\"\>AutoCaption dialog\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145574				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Chapter numbering\"\>Chapter numbering\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Creating a Table of Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147104				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; creating and updating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating; tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147104				0	lv	\<variable id=\"indices_toc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_toc.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Table of Contents\"\>Creating a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	lv	The best way to generate a table of contents is to apply the predefined heading paragraph styles, such as "Heading 1", to the paragraphs that you want to include in your table of contents. After you apply these styles, you can then create a table of contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id5876949				0	lv	To Insert a Table of Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	lv	Click in your document where you want to create the table of contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120211.xhp\" name=\"Index/Table\"\>\<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153746				0	lv	Select "Table of Contents" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146856				0	lv	Select any options that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146872				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146896				0	lv	If you want to use a different paragraph style as a table of contents entry, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Additional Styles\</item\> check box in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Create from\</item\> area, and then click the (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) button next to the check box. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Assign Styles\</item\> dialog, click the style in the list, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>>>\</item\> or the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\><<\</item\> button to define the outline level for the paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153148				0	lv	To Update a Table of Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153161				0	lv	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153183				0	lv	Right-click in the table of contents and choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147066				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - All Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Counting Words				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149686				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>words; counting in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number of words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; number of words/characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; number of words/characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters; counting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number of characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>counting words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word counts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686				0	lv	\<variable id=\"words_count\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/words_count.xhp\" name=\"Counting Words\"\>Counting Words\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D1				0	lv	If you want to count only some text of your document, select the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3149821				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Word Count\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	hd_id1116200901133957				0	lv	How does %PRODUCTNAME count words?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id1116200901133998				0	lv	In general, every string of characters between two spaces is a word. Tabs, line breaks, and paragraph breaks are word limits, too.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id1116200901133985				0	lv	Words with dashes or always visible hyphens, as in plug-in, add-on, user/config, are counted as one word each.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id111620090113399				0	lv	The words can be a mix of letters, numbers, and special characters. So the following text counts as four words: abc123 1.23 "$" http://www.example.com.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E2				0	lv	To get some more statistics about the document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties - Statistics\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3147418				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100400.xhp\" name=\"File - Properties - Statistics\"\>File - Properties - Statistics\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Removing Line Breaks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149687				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>hard returns in pasted text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>line breaks;removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copies;removing line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph marks;removing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916				0	lv	\<variable id=\"removing_line_breaks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/removing_line_breaks.xhp\"\>Removing Line Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	lv	Use the AutoCorrect feature to remove line breaks that occur within sentences. Unwanted line breaks can occur when you copy text from another source and paste it into a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153413	3			0	lv	This AutoCorrect feature only works on text that is formatted with the "Default" paragraph style. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138	5			0	lv	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>               \<emph\>.\</emph\>            				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	lv	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, ensure that \<emph\>Combine single line paragraphs if length greater than 50%\</emph\> is selected. To change the minimum percentage for the line length, double-click the option in the list, and then enter a new percentage.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093				0	lv	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	lv	Select the text containing the line breaks that you want to remove.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156253				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Apply Style\</item\> box on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar, choose “Default”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153388				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect - Apply\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Word Completion for Text Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148882				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>automatic word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>completion of words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion;using/disabling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>disabling;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>switching off;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deactivating;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>refusing word completions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rejecting word completions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	lv	\<variable id=\"word_completion\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion.xhp\"\>Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076F				0	lv	$[officename] collects words that you frequently use in the current session. When you later type the first three letters of a collected word, $[officename] automatically completes the word. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	91			0	lv	If there is more than one word in the AutoCorrect memory that matches the three letters that you type, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to cycle through the available words. To cycle in the opposite direction, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Tab. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078D				0	lv	 To Accept/Reject a Word Completion				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10794				0	lv	By default, you accept the word completion by pressing the Enter key. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079B				0	lv	 To reject the word completion, continue typing with any other key. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079E				0	lv	 To Switch off the Word Completion 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A5				0	lv	 Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Word Completion\</item\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AD				0	lv	 Clear \<emph\>Enable word completion\</emph\> . 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_id7504806				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion_adjust.xhp\"\>Fine-Tuning the Word Completion\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
