helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154248				0	lv	\<variable id=\"calculate_multitable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_multitable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Across Tables\"\>Calculating Across Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	lv	You can perform calculations that span across more than one table in a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147795				0	lv	Open a text document, insert two tables, and type numbers in a few cells in both tables.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147815				0	lv	Place your cursor in an empty cell in one of the tables.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833				0	lv	Press F2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	lv	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, enter the function that you want to perform, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	lv	Click in a cell containing a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147274				0	lv	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
