helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151312				0	lv	Separator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150350				0	lv	Paragraphs are separated by nonprinting paragraph marks. You can also specify that tabs or a character act as separators when you sort paragraphs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154570				0	lv	Tabs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SORTING:RB_TAB\"\>If the selected paragraphs correspond to a list separated by tabs, select this option.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154190				0	lv	Character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159196				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:DLG_SORTING:ED_TABCH\"\>Enter the character that you want to use as a separator in the selected area.\</ahelp\> By using the separator, $[officename] can determine the position of the sorting key in the selected paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151324				0	lv	...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_DLG_SORTING_PB_DELIM\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Special Characters\</emph\> dialog, where you can select the character that you want to use as a separator.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149482				0	lv	Language				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151252				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_SORTING_LB_LANG\"\>Select the language that defines the sorting rules.\</ahelp\> Some languages sort special characters differently than other languages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149104				0	lv	Match case				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154838				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_DLG_SORTING_CB_CASE\"\>Distinguishes between uppercase and lowercase letters when you sort a table. For Asian languages special handling applies.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10895				0	lv	For Asian languages, select \<emph\>Match case \</emph\>to apply multi-level collation. In the multi-level collation, the primitive forms of the entries are first compared with the cases of the forms and diacritics ignored. If the forms are the same, the diacritics of the forms are compared. If the forms are still the same, the cases, character widths, and Japanese Kana differences of the forms are compared.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120225.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Entries (user-defined index)				20200411 15:09:53
