helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Input Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147515				0	lv	Input Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146041				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FLD_INPUT\"\>Inserts a text field that you can open and edit by clicking it in the document.\</ahelp\> You can use input fields for text, or to assign a new value to a variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470				0	lv	To change the content of an Input Field in a document, click the field, and then edit the text in the lower box of the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153669				0	lv	Edit				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154571				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:MULTILINEEDIT:DLG_FLD_INPUT:ED_EDIT\"\>The upper box displays the name that you entered in the \<emph\>Reference\</emph\> box of the Input Field on the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab of the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> dialog. The lower box displays the contents of the field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155897				0	lv	Next				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149691				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:DLG_FLD_INPUT:PB_NEXT\"\>Jumps to the next input field in the document.\</ahelp\> This button is only available when you position the cursor directly before an input field, and then press Shift+Ctrl+F9.				20200411 15:09:53
