helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151180				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:METRICFIELD:TP_FRM_STD:ED_WIDTH\"\>Enter the width that you want for the selected object.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154646				0	lv	Relative				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145413				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FRM_STD:CB_REL_WIDTH\"\>Calculates the width of the selected object as a percentage of the width of the page text area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147516				0	lv	Height				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154099				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:METRICFIELD:TP_FRM_STD:ED_HEIGHT\"\>Enter the height that you want for the selected object.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149809				0	lv	Relative				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154563				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FRM_STD:CB_REL_HEIGHT\"\>Calculates the height of the selected object as a percentage of the height of the page text area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151313				0	lv	Keep ratio				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153675				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FRM_STD:CB_FIXEDRATIO\"\>Maintains the height and width ratio when you change the width or the height setting.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154470				0	lv	Original Size				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155898				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_FRM_STD:BT_REALSIZE\"\>Resets the size settings of the selected object to the original values.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102				0	lv	This option is not available for frames.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149824				0	lv	Automatic				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151262				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FRM_STD:CB_AUTOHEIGHT\"\>Automatically adjusts the width or height of a frame to match the contents of the frame. If you want, you can specify a minimum width or minimum height for the frame.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152773				0	lv	The \<emph\>Automatic\</emph\> option is only available when you select a frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155144				0	lv	Anchor				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153352				0	lv	Specify the anchoring options for the selected object or frame. The anchor options are not available when you open the dialog from the Styles and Formatting window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156269				0	lv	To page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149169				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_RADIOBUTTON_TP_FRM_STD_RB_ANCHOR_PAGE\"\>Anchors the selection to the current page.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151028				0	lv	To paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145777				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_RADIOBUTTON_TP_FRM_STD_RB_ANCHOR_PARA\"\>Anchors the selection to the current paragraph.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155913				0	lv	To character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151377				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_RADIOBUTTON_TP_FRM_STD_RB_ANCHOR_AT_CHAR\"\>Anchors the selection to a character.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150115				0	lv	As character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155863				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_RADIOBUTTON_TP_FRM_STD_RB_ANCHOR_AS_CHAR\"\>Anchors the selection as character. The height of the current line is resized to match the height of the selection.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150693				0	lv	Position				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147413				0	lv	Specify the location of the selected object on the current page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147488				0	lv	Horizontal				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FRM_STD:DLB_HORIZONTAL\"\>Select the horizontal alignment option for the object.\</ahelp\> This option is not available if you chose "anchor as character".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149554				0	lv	by				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145258				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:METRICFIELD:TP_FRM_STD:ED_AT_HORZ_POS\"\>Enter the amount of space to leave between the left edge of the selected object and the reference point that you select in the \<emph\>To\</emph\> box.\</ahelp\> This option is only available if you select "From Left" in the \<emph\>Horizontal\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150545				0	lv	to				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149213				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FRM_STD:LB_HORI_RELATION\"\>Select the reference point for the selected horizontal alignment option.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149230				0	lv	You can see the result of the alignments options that you select in the Preview box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147746				0	lv	Mirror on even pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146337				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FRM_STD:CB_MIRROR\"\>Reverses the current horizontal alignment settings on even pages.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148446				0	lv	You can also use the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060300.xhp\" name=\"Graphics\"\>\<emph\>Graphics\</emph\>\</link\> flip options to adjust the layout of objects on even and odd pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145310				0	lv	Vertical				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150161				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FRM_STD:DLB_VERTICAL\"\>Select the vertical alignment option for the object.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150463				0	lv	If you anchor an object to a frame with a fixed height, only the "Bottom" and "Center" alignment options are available.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154724				0	lv	by				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156130	34			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:METRICFIELD:TP_FRM_STD:ED_AT_VERT_POS\"\>Enter the amount of space to leave between the top edge of the selected object and the reference point that you select in the \<emph\>To\</emph\> box.\</ahelp\> This option is only available if you select "From Top" or "From Bottom" (as character) in the \<emph\>Vertical\</emph\> box. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150912				0	lv	to				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155075				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FRM_STD:LB_VERT_RELATION\"\>Select the reference point for the selected vertical alignment option.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A8E				0	lv	Follow text flow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A92				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"sw:CheckBox:TP_FRM_STD:CB_FOLLOWTEXTFLOW\"\>Keeps the selected object within the layout boundaries of the text that the object is anchored to. To place the selected object anywhere in your document, do not select this option.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AA6				0	lv	By default, the \<emph\>Follow text flow\</emph\> option is selected when you open a document that was created in a version of %PRODUCTNAME older than %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION. However, this option is not selected when you create a document or when you open a document in Microsoft Word format (*.doc).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149241				0	lv	The green rectangle represents the selected object and the red rectangle represents the alignment reference point. If you anchor the object as a character, the reference rectangle changes to a red line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05260000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Anchor\"\>\<emph\>Format - Anchor\</emph\>\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
