helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_newaddlis.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057B				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Adds a new blank record to the address list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_newaddlis.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057E				0	lv	Delete				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_newaddlis.xhp	0	help	par_idN10582				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected record.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_newaddlis.xhp	0	help	par_idN10585				0	lv	Find				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_newaddlis.xhp	0	help	par_idN10589				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/mm_finent.xhp\"\>Find Entry\</link\> dialog. You can leave the dialog open while you edit the entries.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_newaddlis.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059A				0	lv	Customize				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_newaddlis.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059E				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/mm_cusaddlis.xhp\"\>Customize Address List\</link\> dialog where you can rearrange, rename, add, and delete fields.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120226.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Entries (table of objects)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120226.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147401				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120226.xhp\" name=\"Entries (table of objects)\"\>Entries (table of objects)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120226.xhp	0	help	par_id3083447	2			0	lv	\<variable id=\"eintraege\"\>Specify the format for the entries in a Table of Objects. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120226.xhp	0	help	par_id3150017				0	lv	A Table of Objects only has one index level.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Edit Concordance File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148768				0	lv	\<bookmark_value\>editing; concordance files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>concordance files; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768				0	lv	Edit Concordance File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151180				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_CREATE_AUTOMARK\"\>Create or edit a list of words to include in an Alphabetical Index.\</ahelp\> A concordance file lists words that should be referenced in an alphabetical index, together with the page number(s) where they appear in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id837427				0	lv	You can use the Find All button on the Find & Replace dialog to highlight all places where a word appears, then open the Insert Index Entry dialog to add that word and places to the alphabetical index. However, if you need the same set of alphabetical indexes in multiple documents, the concordance file allows to enter every word just once, then use the list many times.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154645				0	lv	To access the Edit Concordance File dialog:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3149292				0	lv	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables - Index/Table\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420	21			0	lv	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>box, select "Alphabetical Index".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154107	22			0	lv	In the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Concordance file\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153668				0	lv	Click the \<emph\>File\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\> or \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470	24			0	lv	A concordance file contains the following fields: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3152953				0	lv	"Search term" refers to the index entry that you want to mark in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	lv	"Alternative entry" refers to the index entry that you want to appear in the index.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154194				0	lv	The 1st and 2nd Keys are parent index entries. The "Search term" or the "Alternative entry" appears as a subentry under the 1st and 2nd Keys.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155184				0	lv	"Match case" means that uppercase and lowercase letters are considered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3143282				0	lv	"Word only" searches for the term as a single word.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3147220				0	lv	To enable the "Match case" or "Word only" options, click in the corresponding cell, and then select the check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153629				0	lv	To create a concordance file without the Edit Concordance File dialog:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153644				0	lv	Use the following format guidelines when you create a concordance file:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3152770				0	lv	Each entry in the concordance file is on a separate line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	lv	Commented lines start with #.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153354				0	lv	Use the following format for the entries:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3149172				0	lv	Search term;Alternative entry;1st key;2nd key;Match case;Word only				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3156270				0	lv	The entries "Match case" and "Word only" are interpreted as "No" or FALSE if they are empty or zero (0). All other contents are interpreted as "Yes" or TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145778				0	lv	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	lv	For example, to include the word "Boston" in your alphabetical index under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line in the concordance file:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	lv	Boston;Boston;Cities;;0;0 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151383				0	lv	This also finds "Boston" if it is written in lowercase letters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155866				0	lv	To include the "Beacon Hill" district in Boston under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3150116	18			0	lv	Beacon Hill;Boston;Cities; 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04230000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Footer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04230000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147403				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04230000.xhp\" name=\"Footer\"\>Footer\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04230000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149353				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertPageFooter\"\>Adds or removes a footer from the page style that you select in the submenu. The footer is added to all of the pages that use the same page style.\</ahelp\> In a new document, only the "Default" page style is listed. Other page styles are added to the list after you apply them in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04230000.xhp	0	help	par_id7026276				0	lv	The footers are visible only when you view the document in print layout (enable \<emph\>View - Print Layout\</emph\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04230000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150018				0	lv	A check mark is displayed in front of the page styles that have footers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04230000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150566				0	lv	To remove a footer, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style containing the footer. The footer is removed from all of the pages that use this page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04230000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153923				0	lv	To add or remove footers from all of the page styles that are in use in the document, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer - All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04230000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151187				0	lv	To format a footer, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05040300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - Footer\"\>\<emph\>Format - Page - Footer\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
