helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153721				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2:LISTBOX:RID_STYLECATALOG:BT_TOOL\"\>These are the different categories of formatting styles.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151271				0	lv	Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153154				0	lv	Description				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172	6			0	lv	Character Styles 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147512				0	lv	Use Character Styles to format single characters, or entire words and phrases. If you want, you can nest Character Styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150713	8			0	lv	Paragraph Styles 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149810				0	lv	Use Paragraph Styles to format paragraphs, including the font type and size. You can also select the paragraph style to apply to the next paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151308				0	lv	Frame Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147527				0	lv	Use Frame Styles to format text and graphic frames.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960	12			0	lv	Page Styles 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155897				0	lv	Use Page Styles to organize the structure of the document, and to add page numbers. You can also specify the page style to apply to the first page that follows after a page break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196	63			0	lv	Numbering Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149298	64			0	lv	Use Numbering Styles to format numbered or bulleted lists.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149821				0	lv	Style Groups				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154828				0	lv	These are the style groups that you can display in the Styles and Formatting window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148977				0	lv	Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149032				0	lv	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153642				0	lv	Automatic				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152769				0	lv	Displays styles appropriate to the current context.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154374				0	lv	All Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153351				0	lv	Displays all styles of the active style category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150590				0	lv	Applied Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149168	24			0	lv	Displays the styles (of selected category) applied in the current document. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156368				0	lv	Custom Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145780				0	lv	Displays all user-defined styles in the selected style category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155908				0	lv	Character Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114				0	lv	Displays formatting styles for text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	lv	Chapter Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	lv	Displays formatting styles for headings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147500				0	lv	List Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	lv	Displays formatting styles for numbered or bulleted lists.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	lv	Index Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155975				0	lv	Displays formatting styles for indexes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149213				0	lv	Special Region Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147736				0	lv	Displays formatting styles for headers, footers, footnotes, endnotes, tables, and captions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146339				0	lv	HTML Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149845				0	lv	Displays a list of styles for HTML documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155560				0	lv	Conditional Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154774				0	lv	Displays the user-defined conditional styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151090				0	lv	Hierarchical				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148448				0	lv	Displays the styles in the selected category in a hierarchical list. To view the styles in a sublevel, click on the plus sign (+) next to the sublevel name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155580				0	lv	Template Management				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145622				0	lv	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Template Management\"\>\<emph\>Template Management\</emph\>\</link\> dialog to copy styles from one document to another.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	While  Typing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436	1			0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05150100.xhp\" name=\"While  Typing\"\>While Typing\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017	2			0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OnlineAutoFormat\"\>Automatically formats the document while you type. To set the formatting options, choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>\<emph\> Options\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>tab.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	lv	You can use AutoCorrect to format text documents and plain ASCII text files, but not characters that you have manually formatted. Automatic \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"word completion\"\>word completion\</link\> only occurs after you type a word for the second time in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147407				0	lv	To reverse the last AutoCorrect action, choose \<emph\>Edit - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02010000.xhp\" name=\"Undo\"\>\<emph\>Undo\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05150200.xhp\" name=\"Other AutoFormat rules\"\>Other AutoCorrect rules\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge00.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Mail Merge Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge00.xhp	0	help	par_idN10549				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/mailmerge00.xhp\"\>Mail Merge Wizard\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge00.xhp	0	help	par_idN10559				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Starts the Mail Merge Wizard to create form letters or send e-mail messages to many recipients.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge00.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CC				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/mailmerge01.xhp\" name=\"Mail Merge Wizard - Starting document\"\>Mail Merge Wizard - Starting document\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge00.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F6				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/01150000.xhp\"\>Configurable Mail Merge dialog\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lv	Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151177				0	lv	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149802				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Navigator\"\>Shows or hides the Navigator, where you can quickly jump to different parts of your document. You can also use the Navigator to insert elements from the current document or other open documents, and to organize master documents.\</ahelp\> To edit an item in the Navigator, right-click the item, and then choose a command from the context menu. If you want, you can \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#andocken\" name=\"dock\"\>dock\</link\> the Navigator at the edge of your workspace.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154475				0	lv	To open the Navigator, choose \<emph\>View - Navigator\</emph\>. To move the Navigator, drag its title bar. To dock the Navigator, drag its title bar to the left or to the right edge of the workspace. To undock the Navigator, double-click in a free area of the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149490				0	lv	Click the plus sign (+) next to a category in the Navigator to view the items in the category. To view the number of items in a category, rest your mouse pointer over the category in the Navigator. To jump to an item in the document, double-click the item in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149106				0	lv	To jump to the next or previous item in a document, click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110100.xhp\" name=\"Navigation\"\>Navigation\</link\> icon to open the Navigation toolbar, click the item category, and then click the up or down arrows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	lv	A hidden section in a document appears gray in the Navigator, and displays the text "hidden" when you rest the mouse pointer over it. The same applies to header and footer contents of Page Styles that are not used in a document, and hidden contents in tables, text frames, graphics, OLE objects, and indexes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149176				0	lv	Toggle				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	lv	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Switches between master view and normal view if a master document is open.\</ahelp\>Switches between \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"master view\"\>master view\</link\> and normal view if a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010001.xhp\" name=\"master document\"\>master document\</link\> is open.				20200411 15:09:53
